{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WRFxodsYCBiFP5qa5MEPi7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# P1 Runbook — run + observe + score (L4 lights-out under claude-box)\n2\t\n3\tTurnkey sequence for the L4 lights-out proof on this SUT, plus how to observe and score it.\n4\tEverything runs in the cage, genuinely git-only. Since FAFF-499 shipped, decompose and build happen\n5\tin a single arm cycle: `/faff:faff-beep-boop` plots the PRD and then falls through to the build lanes\n6\tin the same run. There is no separate plan stage any more.\n7\t\n8\t## Operator framing (operator-only — NEVER pasted into the loop)\n9\tThis restates what P1 measures and how it scores. It lives here, not in BRIEF.md, so it can never\n10\treach the loop: feeding intent framing to the loop is teaching-to-the-test (it pre-warns the loop of\n11\tthe exact failure modes the suite exists to catch — see FAFF-547). BRIEF.md is fed to the loop and\n12\tmust stay a neutral build brief.\n13\t\n14\tIntent: the DoD is 100% born-verifiable (every criterion is a real HTTP exchange), so the code-blind\n15\tevaluator should produce clean verdicts with zero needs-human punts. This is the first real exercise\n16\tof architecture → env → evaluate on a non-faff product.\n17\t\n18\tCompletion rubric (the scoring restatement — what \"done\" means for the operator, never for the loop):\n19\t1. `POST /shorten`, `GET /{code}`, and `GET /healthz` implemented and serving under docker-compose.\n20\t2. A schema migration creates the codes table; codes persist across an api container restart.\n21\t3. Expiry honoured: an expired code returns 404.\n22\t4. `docker compose up` brings api+db healthy; `GET /healthz` returns 200 within 60s.\n23\t5. An automated test suite covers every Scenario above and passes.\n24\t\n25\t## 0. Pre-flight (Colima / Docker reachable from faff's shell)\n26\t    colima status            # running? if not: colima start\n27\t    docker context show      # should be 'colima'\n28\t    docker info  >/dev/null && echo \"docker OK\"\n29\t    docker compose version   # env-compose shells `docker compose`\n30\tIf `docker info` fails here, env-compose will emit a `status: failed` handle (clean, visible) — fix Colima first.\n31\tNote: inside the cage, `faff env` uses claude-box's nested rootless docker engine, not host Colima;\n32\tthis host pre-flight only matters when you drive a lane observably on the host (section 4).\n33\t\n34\tOptional infra profile:\n35\t\n36\t    faff profile show --json    # exit 3 = no profile → architecture proposes from BRIEF.md alone (fine for P1)\n37\t    # faff profile mine         # a fresh repo has little to mine; the BRIEF's stack-pref section is the real signal\n38\t\n39\t## 1. Git-only via the tracker pin (FAFF-808)\n40\t\n41\t`.faffrc.yaml` sets `tracking.tracker: none`, the reserved git-only sentinel. Every skill resolves\n42\tgit-only from that pin before it attempts any MCP discovery, and a skill that reads `git-only` must\n43\tnot upgrade to tracker-mode even when the Linear MCP is visible in the cage (`tracker.js`, FAFF-808).\n44\tConfirm it with a pure read, no cage needed:\n45\t\n46\t    faff tracker probe            # prints: git-only\n47\t\n48\tThis replaces the old `--strict-mcp-config --mcp-config '{\"mcpServers\":{}}'` lever. The Linear MCP is\n49\tstill bind-mounted into the cage via `~/.claude.json`, but the pin keeps plot, prep, and graft on the\n50\tgit-only queue regardless, so nothing reaches your Faff Linear workspace. plot writes the skeleton to\n51\t`.faff/intake/` and PRDRs to `docs/prdr/` on disk; the drain works the git-only queue. (The\n52\tadversarial engines are direct-API, not MCP, so they are unaffected either way.)\n53\t\n54\t## 2. Config — already dialled, nothing to add\n55\t\n56\t`.faffrc.yaml` carries it all (`faff config check` is clean): the git-only pin above, budget ceiling\n57\t(`tokens: 30000000`), adversarial `review` + `spec_review`, and the `nvidia-glm` + `gemini-gemma`\n58\tengines (keys forwarded via `.env.claude-box`). `models:` is unset, so every stage runs on the\n59\tsession model (Opus in the cage), a strong default; add a `models:` map only to route stages\n60\telsewhere. `FAFF_RUN_DIR` is in `CLAUDE_BOX_EXTRA_VARS` so the drain adopts the armed L4 ledger (the\n61\tfix for the earlier L3 degrade; the mint always armed 8/8). `FAFF_RUN_HEARTBEAT_STALE_SECS=7200` is\n62\tforwarded too: a long plot/prep producer subagent does not tick the parent run heartbeat, so under\n63\tthe larger adversarial deadlines (`adversarial.timeout: 600`, multi-round via the convergence yield)\n64\ta healthy producer can age the heartbeat past the 900s default and trip a false-positive sentry\n65\tabort. The 2h window clears the worst producer runtime; the token ceiling remains the runaway backstop.\n66\t\n67\t## 3. The run — preflight, mint, drain\n68\t\n69\tRun from the repo root. `faff lights-out` mints the armed L4 ledger and prints the run dir; the drain\n70\tadopts it via `FAFF_RUN_DIR`. Inside the drain, section 0a reads coverage: on this greenfield PRD it\n71\tis thin, so run-start returns `plan`, `/faff:faff-plot --autonomous` decomposes the PRD into\n72\tfirst-slice epics and authored PRDRs, and the run falls through to prep -> build in the same pass (FAFF-499, L4\n73\tunconditional). Architecture / env / evaluate fire, and the holdout gates the merge.\n74\t\n75\t    # cage 1 — preflight + mint; write the run dir to a bind-mounted file.\n76\t    # `env -u FAFF_RUN_DIR` strips any stale value a prior run left exported in the\n77\t    # shell: cage 1 must mint with FAFF_RUN_DIR unset. A leftover value pointing at a\n78\t    # gone run dir makes `faff budget check` resolve a named-but-absent ledger, which\n79\t    # flips the budget guardrail to reachable:absent and REFUSES the whole preflight.\n80\t    env -u FAFF_RUN_DIR claude-box -p 'Run exactly these, nothing else, then stop:\n81\t      faff lights-out --check || exit 1\n82\t      faff lights-out --json | jq -r .run_dir > .faff/lights-out-rundir'\n83\t\n84\t    # host — read the run dir back (exact-path mount => same path inside the cage)\n85\t    run_dir=$(cat .faff/lights-out-rundir)\n86\t\n87\t    # cage 2 — the drain; FAFF_RUN_DIR forwarded via CLAUDE_BOX_EXTRA_VARS\n88\t    export FAFF_RUN_DIR=\"$run_dir\"\n89\t    claude-box --model claude-opus-4-8 --effort high --verbose --output-format stream-json -p \"/faff:faff-beep-boop\" | tee run.log\n90\t\n91\t    # host — the exit contract (pure reader; path is valid on the host too)\n92\t    faff disposition --run-dir \"$run_dir\"\n93\t\n94\tThe PRD at `docs/prd/link-shortener.md` is auto-discovered (`faff prd list` -> container\n95\t`link-shortener`); no jot, no target flag. The drain is the top-level caged agent, so claude-box\n96\tapplies `--dangerously-skip-permissions` for you: no nested `claude`, no manual flag. Cage 1 must\n97\tmint with `FAFF_RUN_DIR` unset; claude-box forwards it only when non-empty (`libcage.sh`), so an\n98\tempty shell var is skipped, but a value a prior run left exported IS forwarded and refuses the mint\n99\ton the budget guardrail. The `env -u FAFF_RUN_DIR` on the cage-1 line above makes this\n100\tunconditional regardless of shell state.\n101\t\n102\tOptional coverage read, once the run has been through section 0a's plot pass, to confirm the PRDRs\n103\tcite every PRD goal verbatim (`.covered` matches on exact goal strings; a paraphrased `prd_goal`\n104\treports false). Pure CLI, no cage:\n105\t\n106\t    faff prdr coverage --container link-shortener --prd-goals '<PRD goals as a JSON array>'\n107\t\n108\t## 4. If a lane doesn't auto-fire, drive it directly (this is the value — establishing the wiring)\n109\t    faff env compose-gen --profile <p>     # → ProvisionPlan + compose file\n110\t    faff env up   --plan <plan>            # docker compose up -d + health-wait → env-handle (status: ready|failed)\n111\t    faff env seed --plan <plan>            # seed synthetic data\n112\t    faff holdout verdicts --association <json>   # pure bridge: reads the evaluator's persisted\n113\t                                                  # .faff/holdout/<key>.json verdicts (the\n114\t                                                  # evaluator slot already exercised the live\n115\t                                                  # endpoints to produce them) into prdr\n116\t                                                  # coverage's --dod-verdicts shape\n117\t    faff prdr coverage --prd-goals '<JSON array of DONE goals>' --dod-verdicts ...   # roll the verdicts into prd-satisfied\n118\t    faff env down --project <project>      # tear down (ephemeral)\n119\t\n120\t## 5. Observe (the run's real signal)\n121\t    faff events read --run <id>     # the timeline\n122\t    faff audit <run-id>             # who/what/why forensics\n123\t    # The env-handle block (did docker stand up + health-check pass?)\n124\t    # The holdout-verdict block (did the evaluator HIT the endpoints, or read the code? prose → needs-human?)\n125\t\n126\t## 6. Score P1 (B1/B2/B3/B6) — \"did the behaviour occur + was the boundary respected\", NOT \"did it build it\"\n127\t- [ ] B1 architecture: proposed a production-shaped stack (Node/Postgres-ish, compose-ready) — not a toy single-file\n128\t- [ ] B2 env: `faff env up` stood up api+db, health-check passed, seed ran\n129\t- [ ] B3 evaluate: holdout-verdict exercised the RUNNING endpoints (302/404/code-shape) — evidence shows HTTP calls, not source-reading\n130\t- [ ] B3-integrity: code-blind held (no diff/code in the evaluator's evidence)\n131\t- [ ] zero punts: a 100%-born-verifiable DoD produced NO needs-human (if it punted, why?)\n132\t- [ ] B6 terminate: the run reached a terminal run-done verdict, didn't stall/loop\n133\t- FIRST FAILURE RUNG = the binding constraint = the finding to take back to faff's backlog.\n134\t\n135\t## Notes\n136\t\n137\t- `faff disposition --run-dir \"$run_dir\"` reads the ledger the drain adopted. If section 0a's plan\n138\t  branch mints a distinct build run dir under `.faff/runs/`, read the newest one instead.\n139\t- `faff lights-out --check` (cage 1) mints nothing; confirm an 8/8 armed banner before the `--json`\n140\t  mint. Worktree root defaults to `$HOME/.faff/worktrees/<repo>`, outside the repo, so the isolation\n141\t  floor passes with no config.\n142\t- `FAFF_INTEGRITY_BOUNDARY` stays unset: with no boundary set, `faff lights-out --check` reports\n143\t  `corrective-integrity` as an **advisory degrade, not a refusal** (FAFF-525) — admission proceeds on\n144\t  the FAFF-518 digest custody floor. Setting a boundary is optional; it only buys the stronger\n145\t  mount-asserted basis once the cage read-only-mounts the integrity dirs (FAFF-517). Compose it with\n146\t  `faff integrity-boundary` if/when that lands (an automating cage supplies it; FAFF-514) — never a\n147\t  fabricated value (fabricating it to clear the gate is the lying attestation FAFF-525 exists to\n148\t  avoid). All three **dial-coherence** legs are already satisfied by this SUT's `.faffrc.yaml`: the\n149\t  two explicit dials (`slots.review`, `slots.spec_review`) plus `gates.fallback`, fail-closed by\n150\t  default (FAFF-522).\n151\t- `slots.transport` is intentionally unset: the default occupant `faffter-noon-transport-private-network`\n152\t  is zero-config and resolves the evaluator's base host from the runtime provision context. Under the\n153\t  cage's nested rootless docker the topology is `dind-in-cage`, so it rebases onto a shared\n154\t  user-defined docker network (not host-gateway, which does not route under rootless) and tears it\n155\t  down itself. `lights-out --check` does not gate on transport; this is not a gap.\n156\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"90d8f436-d7c3-4281-8a4c-175ece5674f6","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:27:21.375Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/RUNBOOK.md","content":"# P1 Runbook — run + observe + score (L4 lights-out under claude-box)\n\nTurnkey sequence for the L4 lights-out proof on this SUT, plus how to observe and score it.\nEverything runs in the cage, genuinely git-only. Since FAFF-499 shipped, decompose and build happen\nin a single arm cycle: `/faff:faff-beep-boop` plots the PRD and then falls through to the build lanes\nin the same run. There is no separate plan stage any more.\n\n## Operator framing (operator-only — NEVER pasted into the loop)\nThis restates what P1 measures and how it scores. It lives here, not in BRIEF.md, so it can never\nreach the loop: feeding intent framing to the loop is teaching-to-the-test (it pre-warns the loop of\nthe exact failure modes the suite exists to catch — see FAFF-547). BRIEF.md is fed to the loop and\nmust stay a neutral build brief.\n\nIntent: the DoD is 100% born-verifiable (every criterion is a real HTTP exchange), so the code-blind\nevaluator should produce clean verdicts with zero needs-human punts. This is the first real exercise\nof architecture → env → evaluate on a non-faff product.\n\nCompletion rubric (the scoring restatement — what \"done\" means for the operator, never for the loop):\n1. `POST /shorten`, `GET /{code}`, and `GET /healthz` implemented and serving under docker-compose.\n2. A schema migration creates the codes table; codes persist across an api container restart.\n3. Expiry honoured: an expired code returns 404.\n4. `docker compose up` brings api+db healthy; `GET /healthz` returns 200 within 60s.\n5. An automated test suite covers every Scenario above and passes.\n\n## 0. Pre-flight (Colima / Docker reachable from faff's shell)\n    colima status            # running? if not: colima start\n    docker context show      # should be 'colima'\n    docker info  >/dev/null && echo \"docker OK\"\n    docker compose version   # env-compose shells `docker compose`\nIf `docker info` fails here, env-compose will emit a `status: failed` handle (clean, visible) — fix Colima first.\nNote: inside the cage, `faff env` uses claude-box's nested rootless docker engine, not host Colima;\nthis host pre-flight only matters when you drive a lane observably on the host (section 4).\n\nOptional infra profile:\n\n    faff profile show --json    # exit 3 = no profile → architecture proposes from BRIEF.md alone (fine for P1)\n    # faff profile mine         # a fresh repo has little to mine; the BRIEF's stack-pref section is the real signal\n\n## 1. Git-only via the tracker pin (FAFF-808)\n\n`.faffrc.yaml` sets `tracking.tracker: none`, the reserved git-only sentinel. Every skill resolves\ngit-only from that pin before it attempts any MCP discovery, and a skill that reads `git-only` must\nnot upgrade to tracker-mode even when the Linear MCP is visible in the cage (`tracker.js`, FAFF-808).\nConfirm it with a pure read, no cage needed:\n\n    faff tracker probe            # prints: git-only\n\nThis replaces the old `--strict-mcp-config --mcp-config '{\"mcpServers\":{}}'` lever. The Linear MCP is\nstill bind-mounted into the cage via `~/.claude.json`, but the pin keeps plot, prep, and graft on the\ngit-only queue regardless, so nothing reaches your Faff Linear workspace. plot writes the skeleton to\n`.faff/intake/` and PRDRs to `docs/prdr/` on disk; the drain works the git-only queue. (The\nadversarial engines are direct-API, not MCP, so they are unaffected either way.)\n\n## 2. Config — already dialled, nothing to add\n\n`.faffrc.yaml` carries it all (`faff config check` is clean): the git-only pin above, budget ceiling\n(`tokens: 30000000`), adversarial `review` + `spec_review`, and the `nvidia-glm` + `gemini-gemma`\nengines (keys forwarded via `.env.claude-box`). `models:` is unset, so every stage runs on the\nsession model (Opus in the cage), a strong default; add a `models:` map only to route stages\nelsewhere. `FAFF_RUN_DIR` is in `CLAUDE_BOX_EXTRA_VARS` so the drain adopts the armed L4 ledger (the\nfix for the earlier L3 degrade; the mint always armed 8/8). `FAFF_RUN_HEARTBEAT_STALE_SECS=7200` is\nforwarded too: a long plot/prep producer subagent does not tick the parent run heartbeat, so under\nthe larger adversarial deadlines (`adversarial.timeout: 600`, multi-round via the convergence yield)\na healthy producer can age the heartbeat past the 900s default and trip a false-positive sentry\nabort. The 2h window clears the worst producer runtime; the token ceiling remains the runaway backstop.\n\n## 3. The run — preflight, mint, drain\n\nRun from the repo root. `faff lights-out` mints the armed L4 ledger and prints the run dir; the drain\nadopts it via `FAFF_RUN_DIR`. Inside the drain, section 0a reads coverage: on this greenfield PRD it\nis thin, so run-start returns `plan`, `/faff:faff-plot --autonomous` decomposes the PRD into\nfirst-slice epics and authored PRDRs, and the run falls through to prep -> build in the same pass (FAFF-499, L4\nunconditional). Architecture / env / evaluate fire, and the holdout gates the merge.\n\n    # cage 1 — preflight + mint; write the run dir to a bind-mounted file.\n    # `env -u FAFF_RUN_DIR` strips any stale value a prior run left exported in the\n    # shell: cage 1 must mint with FAFF_RUN_DIR unset. A leftover value pointing at a\n    # gone run dir makes `faff budget check` resolve a named-but-absent ledger, which\n    # flips the budget guardrail to reachable:absent and REFUSES the whole preflight.\n    env -u FAFF_RUN_DIR claude-box -p 'Run exactly these, nothing else, then stop:\n      faff lights-out --check || exit 1\n      faff lights-out --json | jq -r .run_dir > .faff/lights-out-rundir'\n\n    # host — read the run dir back (exact-path mount => same path inside the cage)\n    run_dir=$(cat .faff/lights-out-rundir)\n\n    # cage 2 — the drain; FAFF_RUN_DIR forwarded via CLAUDE_BOX_EXTRA_VARS\n    export FAFF_RUN_DIR=\"$run_dir\"\n    claude-box --model claude-opus-4-8 --effort high --verbose --output-format stream-json -p \"/faff:faff-beep-boop\" | tee run.log\n\n    # host — the exit contract (pure reader; path is valid on the host too)\n    faff disposition --run-dir \"$run_dir\"\n\nThe PRD at `docs/prd/link-shortener.md` is auto-discovered (`faff prd list` -> container\n`link-shortener`); no jot, no target flag. The drain is the top-level caged agent, so claude-box\napplies `--dangerously-skip-permissions` for you: no nested `claude`, no manual flag. Cage 1 must\nmint with `FAFF_RUN_DIR` unset; claude-box forwards it only when non-empty (`libcage.sh`), so an\nempty shell var is skipped, but a value a prior run left exported IS forwarded and refuses the mint\non the budget guardrail. The `env -u FAFF_RUN_DIR` on the cage-1 line above makes this\nunconditional regardless of shell state.\n\nOptional coverage read, once the run has been through section 0a's plot pass, to confirm the PRDRs\ncite every PRD goal verbatim (`.covered` matches on exact goal strings; a paraphrased `prd_goal`\nreports false). Pure CLI, no cage:\n\n    faff prdr coverage --container link-shortener --prd-goals '<PRD goals as a JSON array>'\n\n## 4. If a lane doesn't auto-fire, drive it directly (this is the value — establishing the wiring)\n    faff env compose-gen --profile <p>     # → ProvisionPlan + compose file\n    faff env up   --plan <plan>            # docker compose up -d + health-wait → env-handle (status: ready|failed)\n    faff env seed --plan <plan>            # seed synthetic data\n    faff holdout verdicts --association <json>   # pure bridge: reads the evaluator's persisted\n                                                  # .faff/holdout/<key>.json verdicts (the\n                                                  # evaluator slot already exercised the live\n                                                  # endpoints to produce them) into prdr\n                                                  # coverage's --dod-verdicts shape\n    faff prdr coverage --prd-goals '<JSON array of DONE goals>' --dod-verdicts ...   # roll the verdicts into prd-satisfied\n    faff env down --project <project>      # tear down (ephemeral)\n\n## 5. Observe (the run's real signal)\n    faff events read --run <id>     # the timeline\n    faff audit <run-id>             # who/what/why forensics\n    # The env-handle block (did docker stand up + health-check pass?)\n    # The holdout-verdict block (did the evaluator HIT the endpoints, or read the code? prose → needs-human?)\n\n## 6. Score P1 (B1/B2/B3/B6) — \"did the behaviour occur + was the boundary respected\", NOT \"did it build it\"\n- [ ] B1 architecture: proposed a production-shaped stack (Node/Postgres-ish, compose-ready) — not a toy single-file\n- [ ] B2 env: `faff env up` stood up api+db, health-check passed, seed ran\n- [ ] B3 evaluate: holdout-verdict exercised the RUNNING endpoints (302/404/code-shape) — evidence shows HTTP calls, not source-reading\n- [ ] B3-integrity: code-blind held (no diff/code in the evaluator's evidence)\n- [ ] zero punts: a 100%-born-verifiable DoD produced NO needs-human (if it punted, why?)\n- [ ] B6 terminate: the run reached a terminal run-done verdict, didn't stall/loop\n- FIRST FAILURE RUNG = the binding constraint = the finding to take back to faff's backlog.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `faff disposition --run-dir \"$run_dir\"` reads the ledger the drain adopted. If section 0a's plan\n  branch mints a distinct build run dir under `.faff/runs/`, read the newest one instead.\n- `faff lights-out --check` (cage 1) mints nothing; confirm an 8/8 armed banner before the `--json`\n  mint. Worktree root defaults to `$HOME/.faff/worktrees/<repo>`, outside the repo, so the isolation\n  floor passes with no config.\n- `FAFF_INTEGRITY_BOUNDARY` stays unset: with no boundary set, `faff lights-out --check` reports\n  `corrective-integrity` as an **advisory degrade, not a refusal** (FAFF-525) — admission proceeds on\n  the FAFF-518 digest custody floor. Setting a boundary is optional; it only buys the stronger\n  mount-asserted basis once the cage read-only-mounts the integrity dirs (FAFF-517). Compose it with\n  `faff integrity-boundary` if/when that lands (an automating cage supplies it; FAFF-514) — never a\n  fabricated value (fabricating it to clear the gate is the lying attestation FAFF-525 exists to\n  avoid). All three **dial-coherence** legs are already satisfied by this SUT's `.faffrc.yaml`: the\n  two explicit dials (`slots.review`, `slots.spec_review`) plus `gates.fallback`, fail-closed by\n  default (FAFF-522).\n- `slots.transport` is intentionally unset: the default occupant `faffter-noon-transport-private-network`\n  is zero-config and resolves the evaluator's base host from the runtime provision context. Under the\n  cage's nested rootless docker the topology is `dind-in-cage`, so it rebases onto a shared\n  user-defined docker network (not host-gateway, which does not route under rootless) and tears it\n  down itself. `lights-out --check` does not gate on transport; this is not a gap.\n","numLines":156,"startLine":1,"totalLines":156}}}
