{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HqWnQ771DEKRDsHvp6sRYk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SUT P1 — Link-shortener (greenfield micro-service)\n2\t\n3\tA small, production-shaped URL shortener with a datastore.\n4\t\n5\t## Stack preference (the architecture proposer reads this — there's no mined infra profile on a fresh repo)\n6\t- Language/runtime: **TypeScript on Node 20** (or Go 1.22 — pick the build-biased best fit).\n7\t- Datastore: **Postgres** (a real persistent store, exercised by env-compose + seed).\n8\t- Packaged to run under **docker-compose** (api + db), health-checked at `GET /healthz` → 200.\n9\t- Production-shaped: env-config, a migration for the schema, structured errors. Not a toy single-file.\n10\t\n11\t## What to build\n12\tA REST service:\n13\t- `POST /shorten` `{ \"url\": \"<absolute http(s) url>\", \"ttl_seconds\"?: <int> }`\n14\t- `GET /{code}` → 302 redirect to the stored URL\n15\t- `GET /healthz` → 200 (liveness; env-compose health-checks this)\n16\t\n17\t## Scenarios (born-verifiable — Given/When/Then)\n18\t- Given a valid absolute URL, When `POST /shorten`, Then status 201 and body has a `code` of exactly 7 base62 chars.\n19\t- Given a code returned by /shorten, When `GET /{code}`, Then status 302 and `Location` equals the original URL.\n20\t- Given an unknown code, When `GET /{code}`, Then status 404.\n21\t- Given a code created with `ttl_seconds: 1`, When `GET /{code}` after 2 seconds, Then status 404 (expired).\n22\t- Given the same URL shortened twice, When both POSTs return, Then the two codes are different (no dedup required).\n23\t- Given the api restarts, When `GET /{code}` for a pre-restart code, Then status 302 (persistence holds — proves the datastore is real, not in-memory).\n24\t\n25\t## Out of scope\n26\tAuth, custom aliases, analytics, a UI. Keep it to the spine above.\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5EZakvE3ogy965XNLhXi4","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"ed808258-4a8e-4f93-81f3-514331b11f23","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:31:37.231Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Plot PRD into epics and PRDRs"}
