{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FYMg2rXFGqTYQyQcpUnH46","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (37.5KB). Full output saved to: /Users/shftwst/.claude/projects/-Users-shftwst-workspace-shftwst-faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b/tool-results/b58olx2qt.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n---\nname: faffter-dark-methodology-agile-delivery\ndescription: \"Agile-delivery `methodology` lens — answers backlog/build named-outputs through seven delivery principles (right-sizing, value-by-risk sequencing, surfaced deps). Opinionated alternative to the thematic default. Runs as a configured slot, not the user `/` menu.\"\nuser-invocable: false\njudgement_seam: grouping\n---\n\n# faffter-dark-methodology-agile-delivery\n\nAgile delivery methodology lens. Fills the `methodology` slot and answers requests for backlog/build outputs through seven delivery principles — diagnosing problems, explaining them in plain English, and recommending fixes. Surface-only at low/medium appetite — no autonomous tracker mutations.\n\nConfigure in `.faffrc`:\n\n```yaml\nslots:\n  methodology: faffter-dark-methodology-agile-delivery\n```\n\n## Outputs\n\nThis skill fills the `methodology` slot, so it answers the same named-output set — but through the seven-principle lens rather than pure graph structure. That set (the outputs, which are required, which caller requests each, the standard envelope) is fixed in the gateway → **The `methodology` slot**: `ticket-shaping`, `pick-ordering`, `promotion-readiness`, `backlog-diagnostics`, `standup-digest`, `horizon-assignment`, `build-queue`. It also answers the optional `issue-critique` (per-issue lens for `/faff-prep`), `crank-up-set` (ranked not-eligible unlock batches for `/faff-wtf` + `/faff-tidy`), `prdr-author` (a target-scaled project DoD for `/faff-plot` + `/faff-jot` + the lights-out runner), `yagni-judge` (Phase-1 of the upper/YAGNI gate), and `rehome-set` (outcome-led grouping proposals for loose Backlog work, requested by `/faff-plot`) outputs. A caller requests an output by name and receives the answer plus principle-grounded findings; this skill does not know or describe its callers.\n\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5EZakvE3ogy965XNLhXi4","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"672843cb-c62a-4d8c-97bb-7f2b415a1bf3","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:34:05.857Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Plot PRD into epics and PRDRs"}
