{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebnSJRiHq4kPo6wPJQmn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T6a8yuFaguaBnnEtUrkRDf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/docs/prdr/0001-core-shorten-to-redirect-on-a-real-datastore.md","old_string":"## Context\n\n_TODO: the product need this decision answers + the PRD goal it serves._\n\n## Decision\n\n_TODO: the product decision, stated forward._\n\n## Scope\n\n_TODO: what this decision covers (and explicitly excludes)._\n\n## Definition of done\n\n_TODO: the completion bar for this decision (born-verifiable enforcement is FAFF-254/257)._","new_string":"## Context\n\nThe link-shortener PRD needs a running service that mints a short code for an absolute URL and follows that code back to the URL, backed by a real persistent datastore rather than an in-memory toy. This is the MVP spine and the highest-risk work (real persistence plus container packaging), so it is sequenced first. Serves PRD goals G1 (mint and redirect), G2 (codes survive a restart), G4 (packaged stack healthy on `/healthz`), and G5 (automated tests pass).\n\n## Decision\n\nDeliver the core shorten-to-redirect chain over Postgres, packaged under docker-compose (api + db), in this order: stand up the packaged skeleton with `/healthz`, add the schema migration and persistence layer, then the `POST /shorten` write path, then the `GET /{code}` read path with restart-persistence. Language/runtime and datastore driver are the architecture step's call and do not change this bar.\n\n## Scope\n\nCovers: docker-compose packaging (api + Postgres), `GET /healthz` -> 200, config from environment, a schema migration creating the storage table, minting a 7-char base62 code, `POST /shorten` for absolute http(s) URLs, `GET /{code}` 302 redirect with exact `Location`, 404 for unknown codes, and persistence across an api restart. Excludes: TTL expiry, structured JSON error envelopes, and everything in the PRD non-goals (auth, custom aliases, analytics, UI, dedup).\n\n## Definition of done\n\nThe thinnest coherent bar the core spine funds, born-verifiable against the PRD acceptance criteria:\n\n- `docker compose up` starts the api and Postgres, and `GET /healthz` returns 200 within 60 seconds. (G4)\n- `POST /shorten` with a valid absolute http(s) URL returns 201 and a body `code` matching `^[0-9A-Za-z]{7}$`. (G1)\n- `GET /{code}` for an issued code returns 302 with `Location` equal to the original URL byte-for-byte; an unissued code returns 404. (G1)\n- The same URL shortened twice returns two different codes. (G1)\n- A code issued before an api container restart still resolves with 302 after the restart, proving the datastore is persistent. (G2)\n- A schema migration creates the storage table; codes are stored there, not in memory.\n- The automated test suite covering the scenarios above passes. (G5)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":88624,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":540,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5EZakvE3ogy965XNLhXi4","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"f01ab0d6-fb85-4ec4-813e-a401f26a5349","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:37:14.119Z","request_id":"req_011CebnSESMBYc5DFnkV5Gvm","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Plot PRD into epics and PRDRs"}
