{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016TTiqjVipqeDBqcULnJup6","type":"tool_result","content":"=== validate ===\nOK — 2 PRDR(s) in docs/prdr valid.\nNOTE  0001-core-shorten-to-redirect-on-a-real-datastore.md: proposed-uncommitted — a Proposed record not yet tracked (the legitimate authoring state)\nNOTE  0002-ttl-expiry-and-operational-hardening.md: proposed-uncommitted — a Proposed record not yet tracked (the legitimate authoring state)\nEXIT:0\n=== admission contract ===\n# faff contract prdr-admission\n\nThe PRDR (product-requirement-decision-record) admission verdict — the two-gate-bound decision that lets a proposed PRDR supersede an existing one, or blocks it.\n\n## Values\n\n### `disposition`\n\nEnum: `admit`, `propose-only`, `reject`\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `admit` | both gates pass and the mover is not a loop superseding a human-authored PRDR — the supersession lands |\n| `propose-only` | both gates pass but a loop is superseding a human-provenance PRDR — recorded, effective only on human ratification |\n| `reject` | at least one gate failed |\n\n### `authority.actor`\n\nEnum: `loop`, `human`\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `loop` | the autonomous run proposed this move |\n| `human` | a human proposed this move — always by_level:ok |\n\n### `authority.supersedes_provenance`\n\nEnum: `human`, `loop`, `none`\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `human` | the PRDR being superseded was human-authored |\n| `loop` | the PRDR being superseded was loop-authored |\n| `none` | no prior PRDR is being superseded |\n\n### `authority.by_level`\n\nEnum: `ok`, `violation`\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `ok` | no recursive-authority violation |\n| `violation` | a loop is attempting to supersede the PRDR governing its own current increment — always blocks admit |\n\n## Coercion & fail direction\n\nExit codes: `0` conformant · `1` violations · `2` fail-loud.\n\n- an out-of-enum disposition or authority field → fail-loud (exit 2) — faff's own producer emits this, so an out-of-enum value is an assignment bug\n- admit declared without satisfying the two-gate constraint (upper.admit ∧ by_level==ok ∧ ¬ratchet.breached ∧ lower.covered ∧ ¬(loop supersedes human)) → conformant:false","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5EZakvE3ogy965XNLhXi4","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"24f509c8-92bf-41e0-a29a-4ec380ccdb12","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:38:14.035Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Plot PRD into epics and PRDRs"}
