{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cebo2Cfe7L5nJoCbWsq6B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Docker is reachable (Compose v5.5.0), gates are pure functions, git-only. The build environment works. \n\nDecision on execution order: this is a strict greenfield chain (E1→E2→E3→E4→{E5,E6}) where each epic's spec quality depends on its predecessor's actual merged code, and prepping E2–E6 against a non-existent codebase would produce weak specs. So I'll drive the convergence wave loop epic-by-epic in dependency order: prep the currently-buildable epic against real merged code, build it (graft merges to main), then wave re-entry unlocks the next. This is the wave-loop chain-unlock design and yields the highest-quality specs. Everything still gets prepped and built (nothing deferred/parked).\n\nWave 1 begins: prep E1 (establishes the stack architecture the rest build on)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4826,"cache_read_input_tokens":171304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4826},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"281ce5d9-39fe-4da7-9dbb-06b27ddd2c95","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:46:14.901Z","request_id":"req_011Cebo2BVh1Noa3XCbfAXoe"}
