{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeboAUReSkhgMiXwfWybm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KBTm2S3DRbzPBsC5SGQiWc","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/intake/2026-09-01-link-shortener-roadmap.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13057,"cache_read_input_tokens":7186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13057,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XY5XLTrTJcSFTSLGnTsGZB","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"6f3b966c-edaa-4d5e-8bf7-d39f72e41c65","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:46:38.327Z","request_id":"req_011CeboATV6MLajMRhwi49oR","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Prep E1 skeleton + compose spec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KBTm2S3DRbzPBsC5SGQiWc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Roadmap skeleton — link-shortener\n2\t\n3\t- Planned by `/faff-plot --autonomous` (nested under run `run-20260901-002455-lights-out`)\n4\t- Source: PRD `docs/prd/link-shortener.md` (Active), brief `BRIEF.md`\n5\t- Methodology lens: `faffter-dark-methodology-agile-delivery` (value x risk, right-sized, surfaced deps)\n6\t- Mode: git-only (tracker `none`). No tracker containers were created. This file is the skeleton of record; first-slice epics carry stable gitkeys for `faff queue-state derive`.\n7\t- Root container recorded onto the run ledger: `link-shortener` (creative licence: tight)\n8\t\n9\t## Outcome\n10\t\n11\tA running, persistent URL-shortener micro-service that mints a 7-char base62 code for an absolute URL, redirects the code to the URL, honours an optional TTL, survives an api restart, and is packaged under docker-compose with a `/healthz` liveness check. Every acceptance scenario is covered by an automated test suite that passes.\n12\t\n13\t## PRD goals (referenced by the project PRDRs)\n14\t\n15\t- G1: mint a code for an absolute URL and redirect that code to the URL\n16\t- G2: codes survive an api container restart (proves the datastore is real)\n17\t- G3: an optional `ttl_seconds` is honoured — an expired code stops resolving\n18\t- G4: the packaged stack starts healthy and answers `/healthz` quickly\n19\t- G5: an automated test suite covers every acceptance scenario and passes\n20\t\n21\t## Skeleton (initiatives -> projects -> first-slice epics)\n22\t\n23\t- [ ] Initiative I1: Link-shortener service live end-to-end\n24\t  - [ ] Project P1: Core shorten to redirect on a real datastore\n25\t    - one-line: the MVP spine — mint, redirect, real Postgres persistence, docker-compose packaging, `/healthz`, survives restart. Covers G1, G2, G4, G5.\n26\t    - [ ] Epic E1: Packaged service skeleton, docker-compose (api + Postgres), `GET /healthz` -> 200, config from environment <!-- gitkey:gk-20260901-r99do5 -->\n27\t    - [ ] Epic E2: Schema migration and persistence layer (links table for code -> url with created/expiry columns; migration applied on start) <!-- gitkey:gk-20260901-vesiuq -->\n28\t    - [ ] Epic E3: `POST /shorten` mint endpoint (validate absolute http(s) URL, mint 7-char base62 code, persist, return 201 + `code`) <!-- gitkey:gk-20260901-ro9j0r -->\n29\t    - [ ] Epic E4: `GET /{code}` redirect, unknown -> 404, restart-persistence (302 with `Location` equal byte-for-byte; code resolves after api restart) <!-- gitkey:gk-20260901-fab1lp -->\n30\t  - [ ] Project P2: TTL expiry and operational hardening\n31\t    - one-line: additive to the working spine — honour `ttl_seconds` on read, structured JSON errors. Covers G3, G5.\n32\t    - [ ] Epic E5: TTL expiry honoured on read (`ttl_seconds` stored as expiry; expired code -> 404) <!-- gitkey:gk-20260901-h4jfk1 -->\n33\t    - [ ] Epic E6: Structured JSON error responses across endpoints <!-- gitkey:gk-20260901-icaiwz -->\n34\t\n35\t## Dependencies (blocker / blocked-by)\n36\t\n37\t- E2 blocked-by E1 (needs the running stack and datastore)\n38\t- E3 blocked-by E2 (needs persistence)\n39\t- E4 blocked-by E3 (needs the write path to store codes)\n40\t- E5 blocked-by E4 (needs the read path)\n41\t- E6 blocked-by E4 (hardens the live endpoints)\n42\t- Project P2 blocked-by Project P1 (P2 epics depend on P1's endpoints)\n43\t\n44\t## Sequencing rationale (value x risk)\n45\t\n46\t- E1 first: de-risks packaging and the container topology early (principle 7) and lights up the `/healthz` acceptance criterion.\n47\t- E2 -> E3 -> E4: builds the observable mint-and-redirect increment, crossing persistence, write, and read slices in order so the core value (shorten then follow) lights up as soon as E4 lands. E4 also carries the restart-persistence proof.\n48\t- P2 after P1: TTL and structured errors are additive to a working spine, sequenced second because they create no shipped value without the redirect chain.\n49\t\n50\t## Stop-rule notes\n51\t\n52\t- The skeleton stops at first-slice epics. Leaf tickets (individual handlers, test cases, config keys) grow later from `/faff-prep` specs and the bottom-up tributaries.\n53\t- No branch was halted for want of discovery: every epic above has a nameable deliverable derivable from the PRD acceptance criteria.\n54\t\n55\t## Open questions (carried from the PRD)\n56\t\n57\t- Language and runtime (TypeScript on Node 20 or Go 1.22) and the specific datastore driver are implementation choices resolved at the architecture step. They do not change the acceptance criteria.\n58\t\n59\t## Hand-off\n60\t\n61\t- Prep the first slice for build: highest-sequenced first-slice epic is E1 (`gk-20260901-r99do5`).\n62\t- Audit the roadmap join-up with `/faff-map` against this file.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XY5XLTrTJcSFTSLGnTsGZB","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"9bc083d2-74e3-49fa-81c0-3668c5162f5e","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:46:38.336Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Prep E1 skeleton + compose spec"}
