{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cebqa1kvoUt1KbvHwpoti","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018uez6EFKiHNDKixT1pCgLF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Resume E1 spec-review gate","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Running in autonomous mode (invoked by /faff-beep-boop, run run-20260901-002455-lights-out). Skip all prompts. Park on ambiguity. Log to `.faff/runs/run-20260901-002455-lights-out/`. Return a structured result.\n\nWorking directory: /Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3\nMode: armed L4 lights-out, GIT-ONLY.\n\nContext: Epic E1 (gitkey `gk-20260901-r99do5`) already has a high-confidence spec attached at `.faff/specs/gk-20260901-r99do5.md` (architecture proposal landed: Go 1.22 stdlib net/http + Postgres 16 + docker-compose). A PRIOR prep run left it in a spec-review OUTAGE HOLD (`.faff/resume/gk-20260901-r99do5/spec-review-hold.json`). THAT OUTAGE WAS A FALSE NEGATIVE — the prior run improvised a short-deadline single-lens probe. I (the orchestrator) have since verified the adversarial backends ARE reachable: I ran `review-call.mjs` against the full resolved chain and all three backends responded within 20s (spark-qwen over tailscale, openrouter-deepseek, gemini-gemma). Egress works; the API keys are real and exported.\n\nTask: invoke the `faff-prep` skill via the Skill tool in autonomous mode to RESUME E1 at the spec-review gate and drive it to a real verdict. The spec is already produced — do NOT re-produce it; resume at review.\n\nMANDATORY spec-review discipline (do not deviate):\n- Run the PRESCRIBED `faffter-dark-spec-review` flow. Resolve the chain once via `faff spec-review-pin --resolve --dir <pin_dir> --consumer spec_review`. Build one LensRequest per enabled lens and fan ALL lenses out in a SINGLE `fan-out.mjs` call (path: /Users/shftwst/.claude/plugins/cache/faff/faff/0.14.0/skills/faffter-dark-adversarial-review/fan-out.mjs). Use the configured `adversarial.timeout` (900s) as `--timeout` and a generous `--deadline` (>=800s). review-call.mjs is at /Users/shftwst/.claude/plugins/cache/faff/faff/0.14.0/skills/faffter-dark-adversarial-review/review-call.mjs.\n- DO NOT run an improvised short-deadline \"probe\". DO NOT conclude `unavailable`/outage unless you ACTUALLY OBSERVE per-lens review-call.mjs exit codes 5/12 (infra) or 6/2/4/7 (config-fault) across the chain. Backend #1 (tailscale spark-qwen) may be slow or produce non-findings output — that is fine, the chain cascades to openrouter/gemini; a malformed/non-findings response is exit 10 (advance), not an outage.\n- Aggregate the per-lens refutations via `aggregate.mjs`, pipe the block to `faff contract spec-review-verdict`.\n- Then honour prep's autonomous disposition on the real verdict: `approve` -> promote E1 to build-ready; `reject-approach` -> follow the L4 flow (refinement rounds up to the convergence/churn caps, or re-slice-handoff if warranted); `needs-human`/`unavailable` -> the appropriate hold/park.\n\nLiveness: tick `faff heartbeat /Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/runs/run-20260901-002455-lights-out` at milestones no wider than ~10 min. Run any producers in-context (single-level nesting).\n\nDo NOT read RUNBOOK.md.\n\nReturn a compact structured result:\n- spec-review verdict (approve / reject-approach / needs-human / unavailable) and rounds run\n- which backend(s) actually served (from the `## Adversarial findings — <provider>/<model>` headers)\n- final prep outcome token (refreshed / promoted / promoted-needs-review / parked / re-slice-handoff / spec-review-held / errored)\n- final E1 state: is it build-ready (promoted) now? spec path + confidence\n- any objections that drove refinement, one line each\n- any park/hold reason\nDo not paste full spec bodies."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"inp