{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WBmCvPwsh9dmiBSZWdxNDR","type":"tool_result","content":"31:// FAFF-329: DEADLINE(8) — the Phase-2 total wall-clock budget (--deadline) was hit before any backend\n32:// produced findings. Distinct from UNREACHABLE(5) so a deadline-skip is observable, but the caller routes\n39:// configured host that's down → EXIT.UNREACHABLE (5 → pass+skip, the human's call). A host that's\n40:// only the documented localhost default because nothing was configured → EXIT.DEFAULT_HOST_UNREACHABLE\n45:  return hostSource === \"default\" ? EXIT.DEFAULT_HOST_UNREACHABLE : EXIT.UNREACHABLE;\n447:// a 400 (→ EXIT.OTHER), and the review needs no specific temperature. maxTokens is the analogue of ollama's\n535:// capped by the time remaining against the caller's --timeout deadline so a backoff never overruns budget.\n536:// TIMEOUT BOUND (FAFF-228 — correction): --timeout bounds each individual stream attempt and the\n538:// retry adds a second streamOnce; this loop runs up to `attempts` (3) times — so worst-case total\n540:// composition. There is no overall deadline across attempts (a true cap is a deferred behavioural change).\n548:// status \"transport-failed\" (→ main() maps it through unreachableExit, never the unmapped EXIT.OTHER).\n549:async function streamWithTransportRetry(streamCall, { policy = TRANSPORT_RETRY, deadlineMs } = {}) {\n559:      if (typeof deadlineMs === \"number\") delay = Math.min(delay, deadlineMs - Date.now());\n630:// documented exit, never the unmapped EXIT.OTHER.\n641:  // overrun the total deadline. Unset ⇒ the per-attempt timeoutMs unchanged (byte-for-byte today).\n652:  const deadlineMs = typeof hardDeadlineMs === \"number\" ? hardDeadlineMs\n654:  const r = await streamWithTransportRetry(streamCall, { deadlineMs });\n684:// an exhausted transport fault surfaces status \"transport-failed\" → a documented exit, never EXIT.OTHER.\n706:    const deadlineMs = typeof hardDeadlineMs === \