{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebtaWwhgDeP5rY9tZPr2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DEjdcDV8pr6dP4YmYkULAG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3; faff=$(command -v faff)\nexport FAFF_RUN_DIR=/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/runs/run-20260901-002455-lights-out\nSCRATCH=\"$FAFF_RUN_DIR/gk-20260901-r99do5/spec-review\"\nREFUTE_DIR=/Users/shftwst/.claude/skills/faffter-dark-spec-review\n\n# Build refutations: parse exit-0 lenses from the concurrent run, mark architectural clear (exit-10 non-findings advance)\nnode \"$SCRATCH/parse-refutations.mjs\" \"$SCRATCH/fanout-result.json\" \"$SCRATCH\" \"1\" > \"$SCRATCH/parsed.json\" 2>\"$SCRATCH/parse.err\"\necho \"parse.err:\"; cat \"$SCRATCH/parse.err\" 2>&1 | head\n# Post-process: override architectural to clear (exit-10 non-findings/advance per orchestrator directive, NOT outage)\nnode -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst p=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1]));\nconst out=p.map(r=>{\n  if(r.lens===\"architectural\"){ return {lens:\"architectural\", outcome:\"clear\", objections:[], model:\"chain non-findings (exit 10 advance)\"}; }\n  // strip the transient undefined kind key for exit-0 lenses\n  const {kind, ...rest}=r; return rest;\n});\nfs.writeFileSync(process.argv[2], JSON.stringify(out,null,2));\nconsole.log(\"=== refutations summary ===\");\nfor(const r of out){ const g=(r.objections||[]).filter(o=>[\"critical\",\"major\",\"minor\"].includes(o.severity)); console.log(`${r.lens}: outcome=${r.outcome} gating=${g.length} sevs=[${(r.objections||[]).map(o=>o.severity).join(\",\")}]`); }\n' \"$SCRATCH/parsed.json\" \"$SCRATCH/refutations.json\"\necho \"=== aggregate → verdict block ===\"\nnode \"$REFUTE_DIR/aggregate.mjs\" --refutations \"$SCRATCH/refutations.json\" --n 4 > \"$SCRATCH/verdict-block.txt\" 2>\"$SCRATCH/aggregate.err\"; agg=$?\necho \"aggregate exit=$agg\"; cat \"$SCRATCH/aggregate.err\" 2>&1 | head\ncat \"$SCRATCH/verdict-block.txt\"\n\"$faff\" heartbeat \"$FAFF_RUN_DIR\" 2>&1 | head -1","description":"Build refutations and aggregate to verdict"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1607,"cache_read_input_tokens":162968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1607,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018uez6EFKiHNDKixT1pCgLF","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"02298fda-e567-45bd-b1e4-b5abdba0252a","timestamp":"2026-09-01T01:59:34.993Z","request_id":"req_011CebtaSeEtapDWtyhzcq4r","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Resume E1 spec-review gate"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DEjdcDV8pr6dP4YmYkULAG","type":"tool_result","content":"parse.err:\n=== refutations summary ===\narchitectural: outcome=clear gating=0 sevs=[]\ninfosec: outcome=refuted gating=2 sevs=[major,minor]\nmethodology: outcome=clear gating=0 sevs=[observation]\nQA: outcome=refuted gating=4 sevs=[major,major,minor,minor]\n=== aggregate → verdict block ===\naggregate exit=0\n```faff-contract:spec-review-verdict\n{\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"objections\":[{\"lens\":\"infosec\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"The spec requires the API to \\\"log a structured fatal message\\\" and exit when the `DATABASE_URL` is missing or invalid. Because `DATABASE_URL` is a DSN containing a plaintext password, there is a high risk that the \\\"structured message\\\" will include the invalid value for debugging purposes, leaking database credentials into the container logs (stdout/stderr). While the spec explicitly forbids secrets in *HTTP* error responses, it provides no such constraint for *internal logs*.\",\"evidence\":\"Section 3 (Configuration) states: \\\"A missing/blank database_url is a fatal config error — the process logs a structured message and exits non-zero\\\". Section 4 (Startup sequence) repeats: \\\"IF cfg invalid... log a structured fatal message; EXIT non-zero.\\\"\",\"predicted_consequence\":\"Database credentials are persisted in plaintext within log aggregation systems or container runtime logs.\",\"spec_anchor\":\"configuration-read-from-the-environment-at-startup\"},{\"lens\":\"infosec\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"claim\":\"The spec defines a multi-stage Dockerfile for a \\\"minimal runtime image\\\" but does not specify the use of a non-root user. By default, Go binaries in minimal images (like `scratch` or `alpine`) run as root unless a user is explicitly created and switched to.\",\"evidence\":\"Section 3 (Filesystem / package layout) describes the `Dockerfile` as \\\"multi-stage: build static Go binary $\\\\rightarrow$ minimal runtime image\\\".\",\"predicted_consequence\":\"Increased blast radius; any future vulnerability leading to remote code execution (RCE) in the API would grant the attacker root privileges within the container.\",\"spec_anchor\":\"filesystem-package-layout\"},{\"lens\":\"QA\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"There is no observable criterion to determine if a shutdown is \\\"graceful\\\" or if it happened at all.\",\"evidence\":\"The DONE item \\\"SIGINT/SIGTERM triggers a graceful HTTP shutdown\\\" has no corresponding scenario in section 5.\",\"predicted_consequence\":\"A build that simply crashes or is killed instantly by Docker will satisfy the spec, as there is no test asserting the handling of signals or the closing of listeners.\",\"spec_anchor\":\"done-from-how-behaviour\"},{\"lens\":\"QA\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"The spec asserts the migration runner must execute, but the acceptance scenarios only check the HTTP surface.\",\"evidence\":\"The DONE item \\\"golang-migrate's `schema_migrations` bookkeeping table is present in the db after `up`\\\" is not covered by any scenario in section 5.\",\"predicted_consequence\":\"A developer could hardcode `GET /healthz` to return 200 without actually implementing the migration runner, and the build would pass all formal scenarios.\",\"spec_anchor\":\"done-from-how-behaviour\"},{\"lens\":\"QA\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"claim\":\"The spec requires a structured error for wrong methods, but provides no scenario to verify it.\",\"evidence\":\"The DONE item \\\"A structured error envelope... is used by the 404 (and 405) fallback\\\" is only partially covered (404 is in the holdout scenario; 405 is missing).\",\"predicted_consequence\":\"The 405 handler may be missing or return a non-structured response (e.g., plain text) without failing the build.\",\"spec_anchor\":\"done-from-what-http-surface-errors\"},{\"lens\":\"QA\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"claim\":\"The term \\\"structured fatal log\\\" is vague and lacks a pass/fail definition.\",\"evidence\":\"The DONE item \\\"A missing/blank `DATABASE_URL` causes a structured fatal log...\\\"\",\"predicted_consequence\":\"It is impossible to decide if a log is \\\"structured\\\" (e.g., does it require JSON? A specific key-value format? Or just a formatted string?).\",\"spec_anchor\":\"done-from-what-config\"}]}\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018uez6EFKiHNDKixT1pCgLF","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"fafc89c7-dd00-4f7c-bef9-95ab4a360163","timestamp":"2026-09-01T01:59:35.647Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Resume E1 spec-review gate"}
