{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cebtsegm31ZbfEAsmbWuv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hp2gXNqbah3Qsnf6iMhaQr","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/specs/gk-20260901-r99do5.md","old_string":"- The api process MUST NOT bind its HTTP port unless config loaded, migrations applied, and the Postgres connection succeeded at boot (a healthy api implies a reachable db).\n- holdout: With `DATABASE_URL` unset, When the api process starts, Then it logs a structured fatal message and exits non-zero without binding the HTTP port.","new_string":"Given the running api, When a client sends `POST /healthz` (a defined path with an unsupported method), Then the status is 405, the `Content-Type` is `application/json`, and the body is a structured error of the form `{\"error\":{\"code\":\"method_not_allowed\",\"message\":\"...\"}}`.\n\nGiven the running stack, When `docker compose exec db psql` (or an equivalent query) inspects the database after `docker compose up`, Then the `schema_migrations` bookkeeping table created by golang-migrate is present — proving the migration runner actually executed at boot rather than `/healthz` being hardcoded to 200.\n\nGiven the running api, When it is sent SIGTERM (e.g. `docker compose stop api`), Then it stops accepting new connections, drains in-flight requests, and exits with code 0 within the 10-second shutdown timeout (observable as a clean, non-timeout container stop / exit status 0), rather than being force-killed on timeout.\n\n- The api process MUST NOT bind its HTTP port unless config loaded, migrations applied, and the Postgres connection succeeded at boot (a healthy api implies a reachable db).\n- holdout: With `DATABASE_URL` unset, When the api process starts, Then it logs a structured fatal message (a single-line JSON object with `level`, `event`, and `reason`, an