{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebtuTDkG4G3DUR555CmU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017axvshCHmonVxwpkw4nsWf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/specs/gk-20260901-r99do5.md","old_string":"- [ ] The api applies migrations at startup via golang-migrate, treating `ErrNoChange` as success; golang-migrate's `schema_migrations` bookkeeping table is present in the db after `up`.\n- [ ] The api establishes a pgxpool and Pings Postgres successfully at boot; a failed Ping is a non-zero exit.\n- [ ] The api does not bind its HTTP port unless config, migrations, and the DB connection all succeed.\n- [ ] SIGINT/SIGTERM triggers a graceful HTTP shutdown.","new_string":"- [ ] The api applies migrations at startup via golang-migrate, treating `ErrNoChange` as success; golang-migrate's `schema_migrations` bookkeeping table is present in the db after `up` (verified by querying the db, not merely by `/healthz` returning 200).\n- [ ] The api establishes a pgxpool and Pings Postgres successfully at boot; a failed Ping is a non-zero exit.\n- [ ] The api does not bind its HTTP port unless config, migrations, and the DB connection all succeed.\n- [ ] SIGINT/SIGTERM triggers a graceful HTTP shutdown: new connections stop, in-flight requests drain, and the process exits 0 within a bounded (<= 10s) timeout — verified by a clean stop / exit status 0 rather than a force-kill on timeout."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":196869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":523,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018uez6EFKiHNDKixT1pCgL