{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebxMQ92ia4inWhKy8Nrg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the on-disk structure. The turncheck hook makes the constraint clear: under `claude -p`, I must keep this turn alive (blocking, in-turn) until the run reaches a terminal state — I cannot rely on background notifications. My earlier foreground Agent dispatches were correct; the SendMessage backgrounding was the mistake.\n\nThe E1 review agent is running in the background (hold file `ts=02:35:00Z`, outage_holds 2). I'll keep the turn alive with an in-turn blocking wait that ticks the heartbeat and watches the durable hold file for a terminal change (promotion clears it; a re-hold/escalation updates it), reconciling from disk when it settles."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6838,"cache_read_input_tokens":237059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6838},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"54707251-ace8-4055-9afc-5801beb6c2ea","timestamp":"2026-09-01T02:48:31.438Z","request_id":"req_011CebxMLmdDxQGufcFDAG2F"}
