{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Esv8kfDFN16MjP7RWfcZqL","type":"tool_result","content":"=== repo files ===\ntotal 3120\ndrwxr-xr-x 12 hostuser dialout     384 Sep  1 00:25 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 root     root       4096 Sep  1 00:25 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 hostuser dialout      96 Aug 31 19:11 .claude\n-rw-r--r--  1 hostuser dialout    2382 Aug 31 19:11 .env.claude-box\ndrwxr-xr-x  9 hostuser dialout     288 Sep  1 01:10 .faff\n-rw-r--r--  1 hostuser dialout   11623 Sep  1 03:08 .faffrc.yaml\ndrwxr-xr-x 15 hostuser dialout     480 Sep  1 00:40 .git\n-rw-r--r--  1 hostuser dialout     176 Sep  1 02:49 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--  1 hostuser dialout    1646 Aug 31 19:11 BRIEF.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 hostuser dialout   10851 Aug 31 19:11 RUNBOOK.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 hostuser dialout      96 Sep  1 00:40 docs\n-rw-r--r--  1 hostuser dialout 2158052 Sep  1 03:32 run.log\n=== faff binary ===\n/Users/shftwst/.local/bin/faff\n=== .faffrc ===\n# faff config — SUT P1 (link-shortener). git-only, agile lens, lights-out eligible.\n# The two explicit L4 lights-out dials this SUT needs to clear `faff lights-out --check`\n# dial-coherence: slots.review (adversarial), slots.spec_review (adversarial). The third leg,\n# gates.fallback, is fail-closed BY DEFAULT since FAFF-522 shipped (PR #403) — no explicit line\n# needed (FAFF-524 drops the restated-default line FAFF-513 originally planted here).\n# git-only pin (FAFF-808): the reserved `none` sentinel asserts this repo has no tracker\n# relationship, so every skill resolves git-only BEFORE any MCP discovery and never upgrades to\n# tracker-mode even when the Linear MCP is visible in the cage. This is the supported git-only\n# lever; it replaces the older `--strict-mcp-config` MCP-disable flag RUN-L4 used to carry.\ntracking:\n  tracker: none\nslots:\n  methodology: faffter-dark-methodology-agile-delivery\n  spec: faffter-dark-nlspec\n  architecture: faffter-noon-architecture\n  env: faffter-noon-env-compose\n  evaluator: faffter-noon-evaluate\n  review: faffter-dark-adversarial-review     # L4 dial: adversarial second-opinion (was faffter-noon-review)\n  spec_review: faffter-dark-spec-review       # L4 dial: adversarial spec_review (was unset -> single-pass default)\nappetite: high\n# git-only autonomous on-switch: default opt-in keeps autonomous OFF; opt-out enables it.\nautomation_default: opt-out\nintake_gate: warn\nbudget:\n  # For L4 lights-out the budget-ceiling gate deliberately EXCLUDES max_attempts (a count is not\n  # an L4 governor) — the real spend governors are budget.cost (dollars, priced from the ADR-0048\n  # map — FAFF-427, the recommended default), budget.tokens, and budget.until. max_attempts may\n  # stay wired as an optional extra backstop only.\n  # `faff budget check` sums cache_read, so a small tokens ceiling breaches before a build lands.\n  max_attempts: 30\n  tokens: 300000000\n  # cost: 15   # optional: budget.cost — the recommended L4 governor (FAFF-427)\n  at_ceiling: stop\n# backends: namespace (FAFF-523/529) — named entries the adversarial `review`/`spec_review` slots'\n# refs below point at; replaces the legacy faffter_dark.adversarial primary+fallbacks scalar block.\n# api_key_env names resolve from .env.claude-box at call time (name only, never the key itself —\n# the box-env copy step below supplies the actual values, gitignored, never committed). Mirrors\n# faff-root's own currently-served model ids. ollama-local is keyless (no .env.claude-box key\n# needed) — its tailnet host is reachable from an in-cage SUT (operator has run this for months).\nbackends:\n  gemini-gemma-free:\n      provider: gemini\n      model: models/gemma-4-31b-it # /v1beta/openai lists ids models/-prefixed; the served-check is exact-match\n      host: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai\n      api_key_env: GEMINI_API_KEY\n      first_byte_timeout: 120 # hosted first-byte lands in seconds; 120s fails a hung/dead host fast so the fallback chain keeps its budget.\n      #timeout: 480\n  spark-qwen-3-8:\n      provider: openai\n      model: unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4\n      host: https://spark.longhair-escalator.ts.net/qwen-3-8/v1\n      api_key_env: DUMMY_API_KEY\n      # Per-backend first-byte (TTFT) window, seconds. Moved here from adversarial.first_byte_timeout,\n      # which the code silently ignores (first_byte_timeout is read per-backend only, unlike timeout/\n      # deadline). The local 27B's time-to-first-token under the 4-lens fan-out runs ~42-74s (measured\n      # TTFT ~50ms idle, ~74s worst case under concurrent load). 180 is 2.4x over that worst case with\n      # headroom, and fails a hung/dead qwen in 3 min not 10, leaving the rest of the deadline for fallbacks.\n      first_byte_timeout: 180\n      # FAFF-918: bounded reasoning-ON. thinking_token_budget hard-caps reasoning tokens so a\n      # review both reasons AND emits findings (was `reasoning_off: true`, which on qwen suppresses\n      # reasoning entirely and misses real bugs). 2000 is a tunable starting point (FAFF-920); at\n      # max_tokens 32000 it leaves ~30k for findings and clears the empty-out knee comfortably.\n      reasoning_extra:\n          thinking_token_budget: 2000\n  openrouter-deepseek-v4-flash:\n      provider: openai                       # OpenRouter is OpenAI-compatible\n      model: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731\n      host: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\n      api_key_env: OPENROUTER_API_KEY\n      first_byte_timeout: 120 # hosted first-byte lands in seconds; 120s fails a hung/dead host fast so the fallback chain keeps its budget.\n      reasoning_off: true\n      #timeout: 480\n  openrouter-glm-5-2:\n      # FAFF-922 spec-review judge backend. Deliberately NOT in the adversarial.refs refuter pool\n      # below and a stronger reasoner than it — the judge is the higher-authority second opinion\n      # that weighs the refuters' standing objections, so it must be a distinct identity.\n      # Reasoning left ON (no reasoning_off): the judge weighs objections and must reason to do it.\n      provider: openai                       # OpenRouter is OpenAI-compatible\n      model: z-ai/glm-5.2:free\n      host: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\n      api_key_env: OPENROUTER_API_KEY\n      first_byte_timeout: 180 # judge, reasoning-on: may be slower to first token than a reasoning-off refuter, so a wider window than the hosted refuters' 120s; still fails a dead host well inside the deadline.\n      # FAFF-941: bounded reasoning-ON, in the form OpenRouter honours. thinking_token_budget is a\n      # qwen3 chat-template lever OpenRouter does not read, so it left GLM reasoning unbounded until\n      # it consumed the whole max_tokens and returned empty (exit 11). reasoning.max_tokens is the\n      # OpenRouter-native reasoning cap. Carried per-backend here, not in the judge dispatch, so the\n      # transport stays generic (no model/provider branch). Keep max_tokens > this, or it never binds.\n      reasoning_extra:\n          reasoning:\n              max_tokens: 2000\n  openrouter-glm-5-3-flash:\n      # FAFF-922 judge PAID fallback, second in adversarial.spec_judge.refs. Rides out a free-tier\n      # 5.2 outage / rate-limit so the judge stays autonomous under load instead of parking to a\n      # human. Same distinct-from-refuters identity requirement; reasoning left ON like the primary.\n      provider: openai                       # OpenRouter is OpenAI-compatible\n      model: z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\n      host: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\n      api_key_env: OPENROUTER_API_KEY\n      first_byte_timeout: 180 # judge paid fallback, reasoning-on like the primary: same 180s first-byte window.\n      # FAFF-941: same OpenRouter-native reasoning cap as the primary (see openrouter-glm-5-2).\n      reasoning_extra:\n          reasoning:\n              max_tokens: 2000\n  openrouter-gemma:\n      provider: openai                       # OpenRouter is OpenAI-compatible\n      model: google/gemma-4-31b-it\n      host: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\n      api_key_env: OPENROUTER_API_KEY\n      first_byte_timeout: 180\n      reasoning_extra:\n          reasoning:\n              max_tokens: 2000\n\n# faffter-dark: adversarial `review`/`spec_review` slots' reference list — points at the named\n# backends: entries above, primary-first (FAFF-523's ordered-reference form, no \"primary\" key).\n# Flattened to the top-level `adversarial:` key per the schema change on faff main (the older\n# `faffter_dark.adversarial.refs` nesting is retired; a stale local `faff config check` still warns\n# on the flat form).\nadversarial:\n  # Larger deadline for the adversarial reviews. The local studio-qwen primary is slower than a\n  # hosted API, and the default 120s per-attempt clock abandons a slow-but-working generation to a\n  # weaker fallback (the round-3 degrade that helped park the last drain).\n  #\n  # The two review slots treat these knobs DIFFERENTLY (traced from their SKILL.md call sites):\n  #   - spec_review (faffter-dark-spec-review) passes ONLY `--timeout`. It sends no `--deadline`, so\n  #     `adversarial.deadline` below has NO effect on the spec review. `timeout` is its only clock,\n  #     and there is no total wall-clock cap: its worst case is per-attempt x retries x lenses.\n  #   - code_review (faffter-dark-adversarial-review) passes BOTH `--timeout` and `--deadline`. The\n  #     deadline is a total wall-clock budget, GLOBAL (not per-consumer) and SLICED per backend\n  #     (deadline / remaining-backends); each attempt is clamped to min(timeout, slice-now).\n  # Resolution for both: timeout = adversarial.<slot>.timeout || adversarial.timeout || 120.\n  timeout: 900     # per-attempt stream deadline (s); default 120. spec_review's only clock. Sized for a max_tokens:12000 review (~9min at ~22 tok/s) plus large-payload prompt-eval headroom. Was 1500 when max_tokens was 32000 (the empty-out workaround); FAFF-918's thinking_token_budget caps reasoning directly, so reviews finish far sooner.\n  deadline: 2700   # code_review + judge total wall-clock (s), sliced per backend; default 480. 3 refuter backends x 900s timeout = each gets one full attempt (2700 is exactly 3x900, no slack). A fast-failing backend hands its unspent slice back to the survivors (the per-backend slice is work-conserving), which is what leaves room for the fallbacks; the judge is dispatched separately and carries its own --deadline. IGNORED by spec_review (which sends no --deadline).\n  refs:\n    - spark-qwen-3-8\n    - openrouter-deepseek-v4-flash\n    - openrouter-gemma\n    - gemini-gemma-free\n  # Per-consumer output-token TOTAL cap (FAFF-911), reasoning + content. Resolution:\n  # adversarial.<consumer>.max_tokens || adversarial.max_tokens || 2000.\n  #\n  # FAFF-918: this was 32000 as the empty-out WORKAROUND — a big total budget so a reasoning\n  # backend that over-reasoned still had room left to emit findings. thinking_token_budget now\n  # caps the REASONING portion directly (see each spark backend's reasoning_extra), so the total\n  # cap no longer has to absorb runaway reasoning. Trimmed to 12000: ~2000 for reasoning (the\n  # per-backend budget) leaves ~10000 for content, comfortable for a large multi-finding review.\n  # INVARIANT: keep max_tokens > every backend's thinking_token_budget, or the budget never binds\n  # (reasoning would hit the total cap first and empty out again — the exact bug this fixes).\n  # Measured: a 70K-token review needed >2000 content tokens to emit well-formed findings on qwen,\n  # so do not trim the content headroom (max_tokens - budget) below ~10000 without re-measuring.\n  code_review:\n    max_tokens: 12000\n  spec_review:\n    max_tokens: 12000\n  # FAFF-922: the spec-review JUDGE — the would-be-park interceptor at L3–L4. It weighs the\n  # refuters' standing objections and rules accept / park-needs-human / keep-going. Its backend\n  # config resolves under adversarial.spec_judge.* and falls back to the global adversarial block\n  # when a key is absent. `refs` MUST name a backend NOT in the refuter `refs:` above (a distinct,\n  # higher-authority identity) — here the GLM-5.2 backend, distinct from the qwen/deepseek-flash/\n  # gemma refuters. keepgoing_bound caps how many extra rounds a `keep-going` ruling may grant\n  # before a forced park (the SKILL applies a safe small default when unset; 2 is explicit here).\n  spec_judge:\n    keepgoing_bound: 2\n    refs:\n      - openrouter-glm-5-3-flash   # paid fallback when the free tier is rate-limited/down\n      - openrouter-glm-5-2         # free primary\n\nsentry:\n  stall_window_secs: 7200\n  run_elapsed_ceiling_skip_when_live: true\n\ncapture:\n  decision_kernel: \"on\"\n=== docker ===\nDocker version 29.7.2, build a7dcaa6\nDocker Compose version v5.5.0\n=== go ===\nno go\n=== git remote ===","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018GfndhCpfjG5LFggM8UCqh","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"fce719bf-577a-4634-b4c0-0fcd059b0005","timestamp":"2026-09-01T03:33:00.739Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Build E1 skeleton + compose"}
