{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a67050c24d4e98a5f","tool_use_id":"toolu_018GfndhCpfjG5LFggM8UCqh","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-501/-Users-shftwst-workspace-shftwst-faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b/tasks/a67050c24d4e98a5f.output","summary":"Epic E1 is shipped and merged locally to main under the full L4 gate. Final report below.\n\n---\n\n**Terminal token**\n\n- **outcome:** `shipped`\n- **merge_sha:** `da01a8a18742a854d3643a3491adb521a4980086` (git-only local fast-forward to `main`; `merge-record.json` written, `pr:0` sentinel, `merged:true`, integrity `custody-trusted`)\n- **gates:** build/vet/test **pass** — FORMAT (gofmt), LINT (go vet), UNIT (go test) all green via the declared CI-workflow ladder (Go run in Docker; host has no Go). Post-merge verification: **verified-ok** (`go test ./...` exit 0 at the merged sha).\n- **adversarial review:** **pass**. Terminal verdict served by **openrouter-gemma** (`google/gemma-4-31b-it`), exit 0, no findings on the fixed code. Backend health during the run: **spark-qwen** HTTP 502 (both attempts, tailnet backend down), **gemini-gemma** HTTP 429 (hard free-tier quota), **openrouter-deepseek** finicky (empties below ~5k max_tokens; overran a sub-10-min foreground window at 5k). deepseek's first pass raised 1 false `critical` (claimed main.go won't compile — disproved: builds, vets, and ran serving traffic), 1 valid `major` (migrate no-op could mask real errors on the always-empty dir — **fixed**), 1 `minor` (scrub encoded-password forms — **fixed**); re-review on the fixed diff was clean.\n- **holdout:** **meets-spec** (`code_blind:true`, gate exit 0). Evidence hit the **running** compose endpoint over HTTP, not source: `GET /healthz`→200 `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` application/json; `GET /does-not-exist`→404 `{\"error\":{\"code\":\"not_found\",...}}`; `POST /healthz`→405 `method_not_allowed`; both containers `healthy` under `docker compose ps`; migration log strictly before `listening`; SIGTERM→exit 0; non-root uid 10001; and the three fatal-boot scenarios (unset / malformed / unreachable DSN) each exit 1 with zero leakage of the `sup3rSecret` token. No needs-human punts on born-verifiable criteria (the 17 prose DONE items are formatting-classified restatements of the born-verifiable `## Scenarios`).\n- **files created (top-level):** `cmd/api/main.go`; `internal/{config,httpapi,store,migrate}/*.go` (+ `_test.go` each); `migrations/.gitkeep`; `Dockerfile`; `docker-compose.yml`; `.env.example`; `.dockerignore`; `go.mod`/`go.sum`; `.github/workflows/ci.yml`; `scripts/ci-gofmt.sh`. Deps pinned for Go 1.22 (pgx v5.5.4, golang-migrate v4.18.1; latest require Go 1.24+).\n- **human follow-ups (non-blocking):**\n  1. **ADR materialisation deferred** — `adr.mode=offer` and the spec carries an ADR promotion intent (5 decisions: Go 1.22 stdlib net/http, Postgres 16 via pgx, golang-migrate on start, compose topology, 12-factor env config). Non-gating; deferred rather than spend flaky LLM slot calls unattended.\n  2. **Adversarial backend health** — spark-qwen (tailnet) 502 and gemini free tier 429-quota-dead left only OpenRouter serving; worth revisiting backend tuning (deepseek's token/time envelope in particular).\n  3. **SUT setup gap** — the main checkout's `.gitignore` does not ignore `.faff/`, so the live run dir dirties `main`; I worked around it (local `.git/info/exclude` + stash/pop of operator config) but ignoring `.faff/` would avoid the merge-gate clean-tree friction.\n\nOne notable build finding: golang-migrate reports \"file does not exist\" (not `ErrNoChange`) for a truly empty migrations dir; the fail-fast boot caught the resulting crash-loop and the runner now treats a present-but-empty dir as a deterministic no-op while still surfacing genuine migration/connection failures. Housekeeping done: env torn down, worktree removed, merged branch deleted, operator config preserved.","usage":{"total_tokens":321156,"to