{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCyReGNsYhwQs3APqAYcKN","type":"tool_result","content":"240\t**How is a duplicate code surfaced?**\n241\t- Options: a typed `ErrDuplicateCode` sentinel mapped from SQLSTATE 23505; return the raw pgx error and let the caller parse it.\n242\t- The caller (E3) needs to tell a collision from a real failure without string-matching pgx internals.\n243\t- **Chosen:** map SQLSTATE 23505 to `ErrDuplicateCode`. The mapping is a property of a correct insert method, not E3's retry policy (which stays in E3).\n244\t\n245\t## 7. Open questions and assumptions\n246\t\n247\tOpen questions: none. Every decision above is closed; E2 is a mechanical schema-plus-store slice with no open product or architecture question.\n248\t\n249\tAssumptions:\n250\t\n251\t- **Assumes:** golang-migrate v4 and pgx v5 are already project dependencies (they are in `go.mod`: `github.com/golang-migrate/migrate/v4 v4.18.1`, `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.5.4`). Validation: `grep golang-migrate go.mod && grep jackc/pgx go.mod` before starting.\n252\t- **Assumes:** the Dockerfile copies `migrations/` into the image at `/migrations` (E1 does: `COPY --from=build /src/migrations /migrations`), so a new `.sql` file ships in the api image. Validation: confirm the `COPY ... /migrations` line is present before relying on the compose-level DoD.\n253\t- **Assumes:** the E1 startup sequence calls `migrate.Run(cfg.DatabaseURL, \"migrations\")` before binding the port (it does). Validation: read `cmd/api/main.go` step 3.\n254\t\n255\t## 8. DONE — definition of done\n256\t\n257\t### From WHY\n258\t- [ ] The running service can store and retrieve a code→url mapping: after `docker compose up`, a link inserted through the store layer is readable by code.\n259\t- [ ] `schema_migrations` bookkeeping is populated (E1's deferred point): version 1 is recorded after first boot.\n260\t\n261\t### From WHAT (schema)\n262\t- [ ] A `links` table exists with columns `code TEXT PRIMARY KEY`, `url TEXT NOT NULL`, `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()`, `expires_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL`.\n263\t- [ ] The migration is the versioned pair `migrations/000001_create_links.up.sql` and `migrations/000001_create_links.down.sql`; the up file is a plain `CREATE TABLE` (no `IF NOT EXISTS`), the down file drops the table.\n264\t\n265\t### From WHAT (store surface)\n266\t- [ ] `internal/store` exposes a `Link` record with fields `Code string`, `URL string`, `CreatedAt` timestamp, `ExpiresAt` nullable timestamp (nil ⇔ SQL NULL).\n267\t- [ ] `internal/store` exposes `NewLinks(pool) *Links`, `Insert(ctx, Link) error`, `ByCode(ctx, code) (Link, error)`, and the sentinels `ErrLinkNotFound` and `ErrDuplicateCode`.\n268\t- [ ] E1's existing `Open` and `SafeReason` are unchanged.\n269\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqTDGk7NCqbki4NjQ15ayY","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"a5334da5-b394-40ab-befc-bd62afab2787","timestamp":"2026-09-01T05:05:17.756Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Prep E2 migration + persistence"}
