{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cec8tzfxMfc1jPSM9gY6N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MeKUcBBFCt3f6ZWE69DDd4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/specs/gk-20260901-vesiuq.md","old_string":"confidence: high\n\n```faff-contract:spec-readiness","new_string":"## Methodology critique\n\nMethodology: faffter-dark-methodology-agile-delivery\n\n- **Right-sized (principle 4): no issue.** E2 is one migration file plus two store methods (`Insert`, `ByCode`). The schema and the persistence methods always ship together (the table with no methods delivers nothing observable; the methods have no table to hit), so this is a single cohesive 1-2 day unit, not a split candidate. Not too thin to merge either.\n- **Workstream fit (principles 1 + 5): no issue.** E2 sits in Project P1 (\"core shorten-to-redirect on a real datastore\"), an outcome-named container, and carries one outcome — the persistence layer exists. No mixed concerns, no catch-all tickets bundled in.\n- **Surfaced deps (principle 6): no issue.** The roadmap records `E2 blocked-by E1` and `E3 blocked-by E2` explicitly; E1 is shipped and on main, so the blocker is satisfied. The spec's references to E1 code (`internal/store` `Open`, `internal/migrate` `Run`, the Dockerfile `COPY`) all point at merged work, no implicit dep to a ticket that has not shipped.\n- **Risk profile (principle 7): no issue.** E2 is a mechanical schema-plus-CRUD slice on a stack E1 already proved (the golang-migrate runner and the pgx pool both exist and are tested). The one first-time path is the migration runner actually applying a version (E1 only exercised the empty-dir short-circuit), but the `m.Up()` branch already exists in E1's runner, so this is exercise, not novel integration. No de-risking spike warranted.\n\nNo principle violations. Autonomous, high appetite: sur