{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecA7vKjw9xh75ZTdspmV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qbye39M5yagBT7zwCHhJeY","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/specs/gk-20260901-vesiuq.md","old_string":"```\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present\nWhen a Link{Code:\"abc1234\", URL:\"https://example.com/x\", ExpiresAt:nil} is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \"abc1234\"\nThen the fetched Link has URL \"https://example.com/x\", a non-zero CreatedAt, and a nil ExpiresAt\n```\n\n```holdout\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present\nWhen ByCode is called through the store layer with a code that was never inserted\nThen it returns ErrLinkNotFound and a zero-value Link\n```\n\n```\nGiven a running Postgres with a link already stored under code \"dup0001\"\nWhen Insert is called again with a Link whose Code is \"dup0001\"\nThen it returns ErrDuplicateCode and the existing row is unchanged\n```\n\n- The migration and `schema_migrations` scenarios are born-verifiable directly against the composed db with SQL (`information_schema.columns`, `SELECT version, dirty FROM schema_migrations`).\n- The store-layer scenarios are verified by the `internal/store` integration test run against a real Postgres (the composed db or an equivalent pointed at by `DATABASE_URL`), never a mock (see the failure mode above).","new_string":"```\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present, and a timestamp t0 captured just before the insert\nWhen a Link{Code:\"abc1234\", URL:\"https://example.com/x\", ExpiresAt:nil} is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \"abc1234\", with t1 captured just after the fetch\nThen the fetched Link has URL \"https://example.com/x\" and a nil ExpiresAt\nAnd the fetched CreatedAt is not the zero time and falls within [t0, t1] (proving the DB `DEFAULT now()` actually assigned it, not a hard-coded or dummy value)\n```\n\n```\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present\nWhen a Link{Code:\"exp0001\", URL:\"https://example.com/e\", ExpiresAt: a specific non-nil timestamp E (e.g. 2030-01-02T03:04:05Z)} is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \"exp0001\"\nThen the fetched ExpiresAt is non-nil and equals E to the DB's timestamptz precision (microseconds), with no timezone shift and no truncation\n```\n\n```holdout\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present\nWhen ByCode is called through the store layer with a code that was never inserted\nThen it returns ErrLinkNotFound and a zero-value Link\n```\n\n```\nGiven a running Postgres with a link already stored under code \"dup0001\"\nWhen Insert is called again with a Link whose Code is \"dup0001\"\nThen it returns ErrDuplicateCode and the existing row is unchanged\n```\n\n```holdout\nGiven a running Postgres, and a store method invoked so that a query-path DB error is forced (e.g. Insert against a dropped/renamed `links` table, or ByCode after the table is dropped)\nWhen the returned error's full text (including any wrapped driver error) is inspected\nThen it contains neither the DSN nor the database password in any form (plain, percent-encoded, or path-escaped), matching E1's SafeReason discipline\n```\n\n- The migration and `schema_migrations` scenarios are born-verifiable directly against the composed db with SQL (`information_schema.columns`, `SELECT version, dirty FROM schema_migrations`).\n- The store-layer scenarios (including the non-nil `expires_at` round-trip, the bounded `created_at` oracle, and the DSN-free query-error assertion) are verified by the `internal/store` integration test run against a real Postgres (the composed db or an equivalent pointed at by `DATABASE_URL`), never a mock (see the failure mode above). The DSN-free query-error scenario forces a real query failure (not a connect failure) so the query-path error text is exercised, not merely asserted in prose."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1753,"cache_read_input_tokens":173389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1753,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqTDGk7NCqbki4NjQ15ayY","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"3bb144d8-c24a-4ac4-90ed-c4794e297604","timestamp":"2026-09-01T05:21:37.989Z","request_id":"req_011CecA7siyYe1YQpCXktDu5","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Prep E2 migration + persistence"}
