{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C2k73bBd3zTK4rMHaAW2aq","type":"tool_result","content":"283\t### From HOW (behaviour)\n284\t- [ ] `Insert` persists `code`, `url`, `expires_at` and lets the DB DEFAULT supply `created_at`; a nil `ExpiresAt` binds SQL NULL.\n285\t- [ ] `Insert` returns `ErrDuplicateCode` on a duplicate primary key (SQLSTATE 23505) and a DSN-free wrapped error otherwise.\n286\t- [ ] `ByCode` returns the populated `Link` on a hit, `ErrLinkNotFound` on no row, and a DSN-free wrapped error otherwise; a NULL `expires_at` reads back as nil.\n287\t- [ ] No query-path error returned by the store contains the DSN.\n288\t\n289\t### From HOW (idempotency)\n290\t- [ ] After an api restart, the migration runner reports \"no change\", `schema_migrations` still shows version 1 with `dirty = false`, and the `links` table is unchanged.\n291\t\n292\t### From HOW (scope boundaries)\n293\t- [ ] E2 adds no HTTP handler and does not modify `cmd/api/main.go` or the router wiring.\n294\t- [ ] E2 applies no expiry/TTL logic: `expires_at` is stored and read back but never compared to `now()`.\n295\t\n296\t### Integration smoke test\n297\t\n298\t```\n299\tPROCEDURE e2_smoke (against the composed Postgres, or DATABASE_URL-pointed test DB):\n300\t  1. docker compose up -d --build; wait for api healthy\n301\t  2. Assert: SELECT version, dirty FROM schema_migrations  →  (1, false)\n302\t  3. Assert: links table has the four columns with the specified types (information_schema.columns)\n303\t  4. Through the store layer: Insert Link{Code:\"smoke01\", URL:\"https://example.com/s\", ExpiresAt:nil}\n304\t  5. Through the store layer: ByCode(\"smoke01\")  →  URL \"https://example.com/s\", CreatedAt non-zero, ExpiresAt nil\n305\t  6. Through the store layer: ByCode(\"nope\")  →  ErrLinkNotFound\n306\t  7. docker compose restart api; wait healthy; assert schema_migrations still (1, false) and step-5 row still readable\n307\t```\n308\t\n309\t## Methodology critique\n310\t\n311\tMethodology: faffter-dark-methodology-agile-delivery\n312\t\n313\t- **Right-sized (principle 4): no issue.** E2 is one migration file plus two store methods (`Insert`, `ByCode`). The schema and the persistence methods always ship together (the table with no methods delivers nothing observable; the methods have no table to hit), so this is a single cohesive 1-2 day unit, not a split candidate. Not too thin to merge either.\n314\t- **Workstream fit (principles 1 + 5): no issue.** E2 sits in Project P1 (\"core shorten-to-redirect on a real datastore\"), an outcome-named container, and carries one outcome — the persistence layer exists. No mixed concerns, no catch-all tickets bundled in.\n315\t- **Surfaced deps (principle 6): no issue.** The roadmap records `E2 blocked-by E1` and `E3 blocked-by E2` explicitly; E1 is shipped and on main, so the blocker is satisfied. The spec's references to E1 code (`internal/store` `Open`, `internal/migrate` `Run`, the Dockerfile `COPY`) all point at merged work, no implicit dep to a ticket that has not shipped.\n316\t- **Risk profile (principle 7): no issue.** E2 is a mechanical schema-plus-CRUD slice on a stack E1 already proved (the golang-migrate runner and the pgx pool both exist and are tested). The one first-time path is the migration runner actually applying a version (E1 only exercised the empty-dir short-circuit), but the `m.Up()` branch already exists in E1's runner, so this is exercise, not novel integration. No de-risking spike warranted.\n317\t\n318\tNo principle violations. Autonomous, high appetite: surface-only for this per-issue critique (no tracker mutation).\n319\t\n320\tconfidence: high\n321\t\n322\t```faff-contract:spec-readiness"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqTDGk7NCqbki4NjQ15ayY","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"50d972a5-836d-4688-b79a-21ed636c61a8","timestamp":"2026-09-01T05:21:46.124Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Prep E2 migration + persistence"}
