{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecBqeYzinA2kSsubaMcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MG8aF4jjKqbHaYAEj3h7Q9","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/specs/gk-20260901-vesiuq.md","old_string":"**Insert and `created_at` / `expires_at`.** `Insert` writes `code`, `url`, and `expires_at` and lets the DB default supply `created_at`. It does not read `link.CreatedAt` on the way in. `expires_at` is bound as `NULL` when `link.ExpiresAt` is nil and as the timestamp otherwise.","new_string":"**Insert and `created_at` / `expires_at`.** `Insert` writes `code`, `url`, and `expires_at` and lets the DB default supply `created_at`. It does not read `link.CreatedAt` on the way in. `expires_at` is bound as `NULL` when `link.ExpiresAt` is nil and as the timestamp otherwise.\n\n**Validation ownership — E2 persists, it does not validate.** E2's store methods enforce only what the schema enforces: `NOT NULL` on `code` and `url`, and PK uniqueness on `code`. E2 does **not** reject an empty-string code or url, does not validate that `url` is a well-formed absolute URL, and does not constrain the code's length or alphabet — the DB `TEXT` columns accept any non-null string, of any length, in any UTF-8 content. Rejecting an empty or malformed URL and minting a well-formed 7-char base62 code are **E3's** responsibilities (`POST /shorten`); enforcing them in E2 would pull E3's input-validation forward and duplicate it. The `links` table therefore stores exactly what it is handed, and the round-trip scenarios below prove it does so losslessly for varied and long inputs."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":203762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":629,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqTDGk7NCqbki4NjQ15ayY","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"d221c4e1-5ce4-408e-b710-c4552d44538f","timestamp":"2026-09-01T05:44:06.118Z","request_id":"req_011CecBqcid1gN2VACztUt4a","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Prep E2 migration + persistence"}
