{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecEeQG4NH3Z1DCN7JQ9s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LT1DUzGP6mxhReMvhp8H4f","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/specs/gk-20260901-vesiuq.md","old_string":"```\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present, and a timestamp t0 captured just before the insert\nWhen a Link{Code:\"abc1234\", URL:\"https://example.com/x\", ExpiresAt:nil} is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \"abc1234\", with t1 captured just after the fetch\nThen the fetched Link has URL \"https://example.com/x\" and a nil ExpiresAt\nAnd the fetched CreatedAt is not the zero time and falls within [t0, t1] (proving the DB `DEFAULT now()` actually assigned it, not a hard-coded or dummy value)\n```","new_string":"```\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present, and a timestamp t0 captured just before the insert\nWhen a Link{Code:\"abc1234\", URL:\"https://example.com/x\", ExpiresAt:nil, CreatedAt: the zero time (the caller deliberately leaves it unset)} is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \"abc1234\", with t1 captured just after the fetch\nThen the fetched Link has URL \"https://example.com/x\" and a nil ExpiresAt\nAnd the fetched CreatedAt is not the zero time and falls within [t0, t1]\nAnd because the inserted Link's CreatedAt was the zero value and `Insert` omits `created_at` from the INSERT column list, a non-zero fetched CreatedAt can only have come from the DB `DEFAULT now()` — an app-assigned or hard-coded value would require Insert to write the column, which this scenario proves it does not\n```"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4642,"cache_read_input_tokens":219950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens