{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecEguq7TDAXKavB3Zegs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0132qkKGmTMoZMuEV5hMKfWw","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/.faff/specs/gk-20260901-vesiuq.md","old_string":"Then the fetched Code and URL are byte-for-byte equal to what was inserted, proving the `TEXT` columns preserve arbitrary length and UTF-8 content with no truncation or alphabet presumption\n```","new_string":"Then the fetched Code and URL are byte-for-byte equal to what was inserted, proving the `TEXT` columns preserve arbitrary length and UTF-8 content with no truncation or alphabet presumption\n```\n\n```\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table present\nWhen a Link{Code:\"\", URL:\"\", ExpiresAt:nil} (empty strings, exercising the \"E2 does not validate\" boundary) is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \"\"\nThen Insert returns nil (E2 does not reject empty strings — that is E3's validation) and ByCode(\"\") returns a Link with empty Code and empty URL, proving E2 persists rather than validates\n```\n\n```\nGiven a running Postgres with the `links` table already created by the up migration\nWhen the raw `000001_create_links.up.sql` DDL is executed a second time directly against that database (outside golang-migrate's version tracking)\nThen it fails with a \"relation \\\"links\\\" already exists\" error, proving the up file is a plain `CREATE TABLE` and not `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` (a build that used `IF NOT EXISTS` would make this second apply silently succeed)\n```"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2158,"cache_read_input_tokens":224592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2158,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"stand