{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L38VUnw4FyLASgwy2Xzvay","type":"tool_result","content":"=== dod classify (full spec) ===\n{\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a fresh Postgres from `docker compose up -d --build`\\nWhen the api container reaches healthy and the startup migration has run\\nThen `schema_migrations` contains version 1 with dirty = false\\nAnd a `links` table exists whose columns are code (text, PK), url (text, not null), created_at (timestamptz, not null), expires_at (timestamptz, nullable)\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": true,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given the composed stack is up and the migration has applied\\nWhen the api container is restarted (`docker compose restart api`) and reaches healthy again\\nThen the startup log records the migration runner as \\\"no change\\\" (nothing re-applied)\\nAnd `schema_migrations` still shows version 1, dirty = false, and the `links` table is unchanged\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with the `links` table present, and a timestamp t0 captured just before the insert\\nWhen a Link{Code:\\\"abc1234\\\", URL:\\\"https://example.com/x\\\", ExpiresAt:nil, CreatedAt: the zero time (the caller deliberately leaves it unset)} is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \\\"abc1234\\\", with t1 captured just after the fetch\\nThen the fetched Link has URL \\\"https://example.com/x\\\" and a nil ExpiresAt\\nAnd the fetched CreatedAt is not the zero time and falls within [t0, t1]\\nAnd because the inserted Link's CreatedAt was the zero value and `Insert` omits `created_at` from the INSERT column list, a non-zero fetched CreatedAt can only have come from the DB `DEFAULT now()` — an app-assigned or hard-coded value would require Insert to write the column, which this scenario proves it does not\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with the `links` table present\\nWhen a Link{Code:\\\"exp0001\\\", URL:\\\"https://example.com/e\\\", ExpiresAt: a specific non-nil timestamp E (e.g. 2030-01-02T03:04:05Z)} is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \\\"exp0001\\\"\\nThen the fetched ExpiresAt is non-nil and equals E to the DB's timestamptz precision (microseconds), with no timezone shift and no truncation\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with the `links` table present\\nWhen ByCode is called through the store layer with a code that was never inserted\\nThen it returns ErrLinkNotFound and a zero-value Link\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": true,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with a link already stored under code \\\"dup0001\\\"\\nWhen Insert is called again with a Link whose Code is \\\"dup0001\\\"\\nThen it returns ErrDuplicateCode and the existing row is unchanged\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with the `links` table created by the up migration\\nWhen the down migration (`000001_create_links.down.sql`) is applied (e.g. golang-migrate `Down` / a migrate-down test), then the up migration is re-applied\\nThen after the down step the `links` table no longer exists (information_schema shows no `links` row), proving the down file is functionally correct and not just present\\nAnd after re-applying up, the `links` table exists again with the four specified columns\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with the `links` table present\\nWhen a Link is inserted through the store layer with a 40-character code \\\"code-with-a-deliberately-long-identifier-xyz\\\" (longer than the eventual 7-char format) and a long URL containing a non-ASCII path segment (e.g. \\\"https://example.com/über/long/path?q=1\\\"), then fetched by that exact code\\nThen the fetched Code and URL are byte-for-byte equal to what was inserted, proving the `TEXT` columns preserve arbitrary length and UTF-8 content with no truncation or alphabet presumption\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with the `links` table present\\nWhen a Link{Code:\\\"\\\", URL:\\\"\\\", ExpiresAt:nil} (empty strings, exercising the \\\"E2 does not validate\\\" boundary) is inserted through the store layer and then fetched by code \\\"\\\"\\nThen Insert returns nil (E2 does not reject empty strings — that is E3's validation) and ByCode(\\\"\\\") returns a Link with empty Code and empty URL, proving E2 persists rather than validates\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres with the `links` table already created by the up migration\\nWhen the raw `000001_create_links.up.sql` DDL is executed a second time directly against that database (outside golang-migrate's version tracking)\\nThen it fails with a \\\"relation \\\\\\\"links\\\\\\\" already exists\\\" error, proving the up file is a plain `CREATE TABLE` and not `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` (a build that used `IF NOT EXISTS` would make this second apply silently succeed)\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": false,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Given a running Postgres, and a store method invoked so that a query-path DB error is forced (e.g. Insert against a dropped/renamed `links` table, or ByCode after the table is dropped)\\nWhen the returned error's full text (including any wrapped driver error) is inspected\\nThen it contains neither the DSN nor the database password in any form (plain, percent-encoded, or path-escaped), matching E1's SafeReason discipline\",\n      \"class\": \"scenario\",\n      \"source\": \"scenarios\",\n      \"holdout\": true,\n      \"oracle_less\": false\n    },\n    {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LtKDwPDa79StKedeoJZRSJ","session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"11b4c073-ac26-44a4-8e06-a34173f758be","timestamp":"2026-09-01T06:55:39.787Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Build E2 migration + store"}
