ound-trip byte-for-byte\n  code match=true, url match=true (https://example.com/über/long/path?q=1), len=44\n\nS9 MET — empty-string code+url persisted (E2 does not validate)\n  INSERT ('','') succeeds; row present with empty code and url\n\nS10 MET — links table is a real table a plain CREATE collides with\n  CREATE TABLE links (...) again -> ERROR relation \"links\" already exists (running-stack observable of the plain-CREATE / not-IF-NOT-EXISTS property)\n\nS7 NEEDS-HUMAN — down-migration file correctness\n  The scenario asserts applying the shipped 000001_create_links.down.sql drops the table and re-applying up restores it. The running stack (api runs UP only at startup; no down trigger; no migration-file access code-blind) exposes NO surface to apply the shipped down file. Fail-closed to needs-human. (Independently verified by graft's internal/store down/up integration test.)\n\nS11 (holdout) NEEDS-HUMAN — query-path DSN-free error\n  The scenario forces a store query-path error (Insert/ByCode against a dropped table) and inspects the store method's RETURNED error text for DSN/password leakage. The running api exposes only /healthz (shallow, no query) and no HTTP endpoint invokes Insert/ByCode, so no query-path error can be triggered through the running stack. The connect-path DSN scrubbing (E1's SafeReason) is startup-observable, but the E2 query-path is not. Fail-closed to needs-human. (Independently verified by graft's internal/store TestQueryPathErrorCarriesNoDSN.)\n\nDERIVATION: 10 met + 2 needs-human -> aggregate = needs-human (any needs-human criterion forces needs-human; canonical per faff contract holdout-verdict).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7021,"cache_read_input_tokens":248434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7021,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available