{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecKHtAqQsQYJ18PBPV3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G3SwpbMuvEdn8ECF7W57ev","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/.claude/projects/-Users-shftwst-workspace-shftwst-faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/memory/headless-turn-survival.md","content":"---\nname: headless-turn-survival\ndescription: Under headless claude -p (claude-box lights-out), the beep-boop orchestrator turn must stay alive until the run is terminal; background agents get reaped\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nRunning `/faff-beep-boop` under headless `claude -p` (claude-box L4 lights-out): the orchestrator turn must NOT end until the run reaches a terminal state (all epics shipped/parked, budget fired, or a closed run with owner.status:done). A `faff turncheck` Stop hook enforces this: ending a turn while `owner.status:\"running\"` with no terminal outcome kills the cage and the run dies mid-flight.\n\n**Why:** headless turn-end exits the cage; there is no re-invocation on background-task completion the way an interactive session gets.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Dispatch heavy sub-skills (prep, graft) as FOREGROUND Agent calls (`run_in_background: false`) so the turn blocks until they fully complete.\n- Do NOT use `SendMessage` to a background agent and then end the turn — it backgrounds the agent, and if the turn ends the run dies. If you must wait on a background/long op, keep the turn alive with back-to-back blocking Bash waits (`timeout: 600000` max, poll on-disk state), and reconcile from durable artifacts, never the agent transcript.\n- Subagents must run long fan-outs (spec-review `fan-out.mjs`) SYNCHRONOUSLY in their own turn; if a subagent backgrounds a fan-out and returns, the detached child is reaped and the fan-out dies (0-byte output). Instruct subagents explicitly to block in-turn.\n- Close the run explicitly at the end: set `owner.status:\"done\"` + `stop_reason`, emit run-end + ledger-write events, stop the sentry-poller. Related: [[faff-sut-p1-l4-findings]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1684,"cache_read_input_tokens":374804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1684},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"bcae4414-1631-4f91-88d8-19ecdfd0e990","timestamp":"2026-09-01T07:21:52.065Z","request_id":"req_011CecKHriHMmcFLkHWmdZtH"}
