e from durable artifacts, never the agent transcript.\n- Subagents must run long fan-outs (spec-review `fan-out.mjs`) SYNCHRONOUSLY in their own turn; if a subagent backgrounds a fan-out and returns, the detached child is reaped and the fan-out dies (0-byte output). Instruct subagents explicitly to block in-turn.\n- Close the run explicitly at the end: set `owner.status:\"done\"` + `stop_reason`, emit run-end + ledger-write events, stop the sentry-poller. Related: [[faff-sut-p1-l4-findings]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecKHtAqQsQYJ18PBPV3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B33UkctZjSzutQK1UKUzWH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/shftwst/.claude/projects/-Users-shftwst-workspace-shftwst-faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/memory/faff-sut-p1-l4-findings.md","content":"---\nname: faff-sut-p1-l4-findings\ndescription: This repo is an L4 lights-out proof SUT (link-shortener); key findings from the 2026-09-01 run about the code-blind holdout vs spec-review tiering\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3` is a system-under-test harness that exercises faff's L4 lights-out chain (architecture then env then evaluate) on a non-faff product, git-only (`tracking.tracker: none`). BRIEF.md is the neutral build brief fed to the loop; RUNBOOK.md is operator-only and must NEVER be read by the loop (teaching-to-the-test).\n\nRun `run-20260901-002455-lights-out` (2026-09-01) result:\n- E1 (skeleton + compose + /healthz) SHIPPED end-to-end through the full L4 gate with a real code-blind holdout hitting running HTTP endpoints, zero punts. Core proof achieved.\n- E2 (migration + store layer) built and gate-green but PARKED at the fail-closed L4 holdout merge floor (needs-human), which correctly refused the merge.\n- **Binding-constraint finding:** the code-blind holdout (running-stack-only) and the spec-review QA lens (accepts integration-test-level checks) have inconsistent definitions of \"born-verifiable\". A store-layer epic split from the endpoint epics is too fine-grained for independent code-blind holdout verification, and the QA lens can force a permanently-unverifiable criterion (e.g. down-migration correctness, which the running stack never runs) into the holdout DoD, making the epic permanently unmergeable at L4. E3 to E6 were blocked by E2's non-merge; run escalated product-incomplete.\n- **Secondary:** adversarial spec-review is the throughput bottleneck (gemini/gemma 429s under 4-lens fan-out; spark-qwen tailnet 502s; openrouter/deepseek often empty). ~3-4 rounds/epic at ~10-20 min/round. Backends DO work; a subagent once falsely reported outage by improvising a short-deadline probe instead of the prescribed fan-out.\n\nDo not override the fail-closed L4 merge floor to force a merge; a holdout needs-human is the guardrail working. See [[headless-turn-survival]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1684,"cache_read_input_tokens":374804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1684},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21bdc136-befe-4bc5-9026-5312f63ae86b","uuid":"82acb51a-9aa6-4096-80c3-d5d0860cd2bc","timestamp":"2026-09-01T07:22:04.408Z","request_id":"req_011CecKHriHMmcFLkHWmdZtH"}
