rl -s -D- http://localhost:8080/healthz\necho; echo \"=== 404 ===\"; curl -s -o /tmp/nf -w 'http=%{http_code} ctype=%{content_type}\\n' http://localhost:8080/does-not-exist; cat /tmp/nf; echo\necho \"=== 405 ===\"; curl -s -X POST -o /tmp/mn -w 'http=%{http_code} ctype=%{content_type}\\n' http://localhost:8080/healthz; cat /tmp/mn; echo\necho \"=== logs ===\"; docker compose logs api 2>&1 | grep -E 'migrate|listening'","description":"Exercise endpoints and check logs (sandbox off)","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01E1fccsUGhjeJKY4JJBDwF1","tool_input":{"command":"curl -s http://localhost:8080/does-not-exist; echo \" [404 above]\"; curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/healthz; echo \" [405 above]\"","description":"Fetch 404 and 405 bodies via host curl","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DpippKMRYKFvss3VudiaNQ","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3\nfaff=$(command -v faff || echo \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-$HOME/.claude}/skills/faff/bin/faff\")\necho \"=== merge-record E1 ===\"; cat \"$FAFF_RUN_DIR/gk-20260901-r99do5/merge-record.json\" 2>&1 | node -e 'try{const d=JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(0));console.log(\"merged:\",d.merged,\"pr:\",d.pr,\"head_sha:\",d.head_sha,\"integrity:\",d.integrity||d.custody)}catch(e){console.log(\"(no/again)\",e.message)}' 2>&1\necho \"=== git main HEAD + ancestry check ===\"; git -C . log --oneline -3 2>&1\ngit merge-base --is-ancestor da01a8a18742a854d3643a3491adb521a4980086 HEAD 2>&1 && echo \"E1 sha IS ancestor of main HEAD\" || echo \"E1 sha NOT ancestor (checking if HEAD==sha)\"\necho \"=== code on main? ===\"; ls cmd/api/main.go docker-compose.yml Dockerfile go.mod 2>&1\necho \"=== git status (clean tree?) ===\"; git status --short 2>&1 | head","description":"Reconcile E1 merge against git ground truth"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01U3MRrcaUy5CspzmJnXvZSP","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/shftwst/workspace/shftwst/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3\nfaff heartbeat \"$PWD/.faff/runs/run-20260901-002455-lights-out\" --unit gk-20260901-vesiuq >/dev/null 2>&1\nwt=\"/Users/shftwst/.faff/worktrees/faff-sut-p1-link-shortener-l4-3/gk-20260901-vesiuq-links-table-and-store\"\ncd \"$wt\"\necho \"=== env slot: docker compose up api+db (holdout env) ===\"\ndocker compose -p e2holdout up -d --build 2>&1 | tail -6\nfor i in $(seq 1 40); do\n  st=$(docker inspect -f '{{.State.Health.Status}}' e2holdout-api-1 2>/dev/null || echo none)\n  if [ \"$st\" = \"healthy\" ]; then echo \"api healthy after ${i}s\"; break; fi\n  sleep 2\ndone\necho \"=== env-handle ===\"\necho \"api endpoint: http://localhost:8080/healthz\"\ncurl -s http://localhost:8080/healthz; echo\ndocker compose -p e2holdout ps --format '{{.Name}} {{.Status}}'","description":"Provision holdout env (compose api+db)"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The run is complete and closed in a proper terminal state. Here is the final report.\n\n## Beep-boop run complete — `run-20260901-002455-lights-out` (L4 lights-out, git-only)\n\n**Stop reason: product-incomplete** · Duration ~6h55m · Spend 41.4M tokens / $39.95 · 2 build attempts · Sentry: 0 trips · runcheck clean · ground-truth reconcile pass · disposition **needs-attention**.\n\n### What happened\n\n| Epic | Result |\n|---|---|\n| E1 skeleton + compose + `/healthz` | **Shipped** (local merge `da01a8a`) |\n| E2 migration + store layer | **Parked** at the L4 holdout merge floor |\n| E3 POST /shorten, E4 GET /{code}, E5 TTL, E6 errors | **Blocked** by E2's non-merge |\n\n**Section 0a** resolved to `plan` on the greenfield PRD, plotted 6 epics across 2 projects, then fell through to build in the same run.\n\n**E1 is the headline: the full L4 chain worked.** Go 1.22 + Postgres 16 under docker-compose, built through gates + adversarial review, then a genuine **code-blind holdout that hit the running HTTP endpoints** (healthz 200, 404, 405, container health, migration ordering, SIGTERM, non-root uid, DSN-leak scenarios) with **zero needs-human punts**, then merged. That is architecture then env then evaluate proven on a non-faff product.\n\n### The binding constraint (the finding to take back to faff's backlog)\n\nE2 was built correctly (gates green, 11/11 store integration tests against real Postgres, adversarial review pass), but the **code-blind holdout returned needs-human on 2 of 12 criteria and the fail-closed L4 merge floor correctly refused to merge**. I did not override it, and no `met` verdict was fabricated. The two criteria:\n\n1. **Down-migration correctness** — the running stack only runs UP migrations, and a code-blind evaluator has no file access, so this is permanently un-verifiable via the running stack. It is an integration-tier criterion the spec-review QA lens mis-classified into the code-blind holdout DoD.\n2. **Query-path DSN-free error** — E2 exposes no endpoint invoking the store, so it is only verifiable once E3/E4 add the HTTP surface.\n\nRoot cause: spec-review's notion of \"born-verifiable\" (accepts integration-test-level checks) is inconsistent with the code-blind holdout's (running-stack-only). A store-layer epic split from the endpoint epics is too fine-grained for independent code-blind holdout verification. Recommended fix: have `faff dod classify` / the QA lens separate running-stack-verifiable criteria from integration-tier ones, or treat store + first-endpoint as one holdout-verifiable slice at decompose time.\n\n### Secondary findings\n\n- **Adversarial review is the throughput bottleneck.** gemini/gemma (the effective workhorse) 429s under concurrent 4-lens fan-out; spark-qwen (tailnet) intermittently 502s; openrouter/deepseek often returns empty. Roughly 3 to 4 rounds per epic at 10 to 20 minutes each. The backends do work; one subagent falsely reported an outage by improvising a short-deadline probe instead of the prescribed `fan-out.mjs` flow.\n- **Install health is not clean:** 31 faff skills missing from `~/.agents/skills` (run `faff sync` on the host).\n- `.gitignore` does not ignore `.faff/` (worked around locally).\n\nFull detail in `.faff/runs/run-20260901-002455-lights-out/summary.md` and `gk-20260901-vesiuq/park.md`. Exit contract: `faff disposition --run-dir <run>` reads needs-attention.\n\n### To unblock E3 to E6\n\nConfirm the down-migration criterion is integration-test-covered and re-tier it out of E2's code-blind holdout DoD (and hand the query-path-error criterion to E3's holdout), then E2 merges on its 10 met criteria and the chain can proceed. That re-tiering is a human judgment call, which is exactly what the holdout's needs-human is asking for.","ttft_ms":9567,"ttft_stream_ms":5728,"time_to_request_ms":33,"type":"result","duration_ms":25173204,"uuid":"124c9077-84d4-4f3b-9c0c-be2a654e2242"}
